WEBVTT

00:02:43.012 --> 00:02:45.742
<i>The hills are alive</i>

00:02:46.049 --> 00:02:50.418
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:02:50.687 --> 00:02:53.121
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

00:02:53.423 --> 00:02:58.258
<i>For a thousand years</i>

00:02:58.528 --> 00:03:01.691
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

00:03:01.931 --> 00:03:06.459
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:03:06.736 --> 00:03:13.904
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:19.279
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

00:03:19.549 --> 00:03:22.609
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:27.119
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:31.326
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

00:03:31.594 --> 00:03:35.086
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

00:03:35.331 --> 00:03:38.823
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

00:03:39.102 --> 00:03:42.970
<i>To sing through the night</i>

00:03:43.239 --> 00:03:47.005
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

00:03:47.343 --> 00:03:52.975
<i>I go to the hills</i>

00:03:53.182 --> 00:03:59.348
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

00:03:59.622 --> 00:04:03.490
<i>I know I will hear</i>

00:04:03.693 --> 00:04:08.187
<i>What I've heard before</i>

00:04:08.464 --> 00:04:13.197
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

00:04:13.436 --> 00:04:21.207
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:04:22.278 --> 00:04:27.443
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:36.615
<i>...once more</i>

00:09:18.674 --> 00:09:23.634
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:23.913 --> 00:09:28.577
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:30.786 --> 00:09:32.845
- Reverend Mother.
- Sister Bernice.

00:09:33.089 --> 00:09:35.717
- I simply cannot find her.
- Maria?

00:09:36.792 --> 00:09:38.089
She's missing again.

00:09:39.028 --> 00:09:41.394
We should've put a cowbell
around her neck.

00:09:41.631 --> 00:09:44.691
Have you tried the barn? You know
how much she adores the animals.

00:09:44.967 --> 00:09:47.697
I have looked everywhere.
In all of the usual places.

00:09:47.903 --> 00:09:50.133
Sister, considering it's Maria...

00:09:50.439 --> 00:09:53.033
...I suggest you look in someplace
unusual.

00:09:58.314 --> 00:09:59.611
Well, Reverend Mother...

00:09:59.882 --> 00:10:02.442
...I hope this new infraction ends
whatever doubts...

00:10:02.718 --> 00:10:05.949
...you may still have
about Maria's future here.

00:10:06.155 --> 00:10:10.216
I always try to keep faith
in my doubts, Sister Berthe.

00:10:10.459 --> 00:10:13.326
After all, the wool of a black sheep
is just as warm.

00:10:13.562 --> 00:10:17.896
We are not talking about sheep,
black or white, Sister Margaretta.

00:10:18.134 --> 00:10:21.570
Of all the candidates for
the novitiate, Maria is the least...

00:10:21.837 --> 00:10:24.328
Children, children.

00:10:24.807 --> 00:10:28.766
We were speculating about
the qualifications of our postulants.

00:10:29.412 --> 00:10:32.404
The Mistress of Novices
and the Mistress of Postulants...

00:10:32.648 --> 00:10:37.950
...were trying to help me
by expressing opposite points of view.

00:10:38.187 --> 00:10:41.247
Tell me, Sister Catherine,
what do you think of Maria?

00:10:41.457 --> 00:10:44.517
She's a wonderful girl,
some of the time.

00:10:45.494 --> 00:10:48.588
- Sister Agatha?
- It's very easy to like Maria...

00:10:48.831 --> 00:10:51.356
...except when it's difficult.

00:10:51.667 --> 00:10:55.228
- And you, Sister Sophia?
- Oh, I love her very dearly.

00:10:55.438 --> 00:10:58.373
But she always seems to be
in trouble, doesn't she?

00:10:58.607 --> 00:11:00.199
Exactly what I say.

00:11:00.676 --> 00:11:03.144
<i>She climbs a tree and scrapes her knee</i>

00:11:03.346 --> 00:11:05.041
<i>Her dress has got a tear</i>

00:11:05.715 --> 00:11:09.879
<i>She waltzes on her way to Mass</i>
<i>And whistles on the stair</i>

00:11:10.519 --> 00:11:15.013
<i>And underneath her wimple</i>
<i>She has curlers in her hair</i>

00:11:15.291 --> 00:11:19.887
<i>I've even heard her singing</i>
<i>In the abbey</i>

00:11:20.129 --> 00:11:22.120
<i>She's always late for chapel</i>

00:11:22.365 --> 00:11:24.629
<i>But her penitence is real</i>

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:27.232
<i>She's always late for everything</i>

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.495
<i>Except for every meal</i>

00:11:29.872 --> 00:11:34.571
<i>I hate to have to say it</i>
<i>But I very firmly feel</i>

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:39.247
<i>Maria's not an asset to the abbey</i>

00:11:39.749 --> 00:11:42.240
<i>I'd like to say a word in her behalf</i>

00:11:42.518 --> 00:11:43.849
Say it, Sister Margaretta.

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.679
<i>Maria makes me laugh</i>

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:55.496
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:11:55.765 --> 00:11:59.565
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:11:59.869 --> 00:12:03.202
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:12:03.739 --> 00:12:04.831
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

00:12:05.074 --> 00:12:06.405
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>- A clown</i>

00:12:08.043 --> 00:12:11.774
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:12:12.047 --> 00:12:15.505
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:12:15.918 --> 00:12:19.615
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

00:12:20.189 --> 00:12:23.681
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:12:23.926 --> 00:12:28.022
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:12:28.531 --> 00:12:34.060
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:39.731
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:44.302
<i>When I'm with her I'm confused</i>
<i>Out of focus and bemused</i>

00:12:44.613 --> 00:12:48.049
<i>And I never know exactly where I am</i>

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:51.583
<i>- Unpredictable as weather</i>
<i>- She's as flighty as a feather</i>

00:12:51.954 --> 00:12:53.785
<i>- She's a darling</i>
<i>- She's a demon</i>

00:12:53.989 --> 00:12:55.320
<i>She's a lamb</i>

00:12:55.724 --> 00:12:59.387
<i>She'll out pester any pest</i>
<i>Drive a hornet from its nest</i>

00:12:59.595 --> 00:13:02.894
<i>She can throw a whirling dervish</i>
<i>Out of whirl</i>

00:13:03.466 --> 00:13:06.993
<i>- She is gentle, she is wild</i>
<i>- She's a riddle, she's a child</i>

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:10.130
<i>- She's a headache</i>
<i>- She's an angel</i>

00:13:10.339 --> 00:13:14.241
<i>She's a girl</i>

00:13:14.977 --> 00:13:18.913
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:13:19.148 --> 00:13:22.845
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:13:23.152 --> 00:13:26.644
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:13:26.922 --> 00:13:28.913
<i>- A flibbertigibbet</i>
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>

00:13:29.158 --> 00:13:30.785
<i>A clown</i>

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:34.991
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:13:35.264 --> 00:13:38.756
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:13:38.968 --> 00:13:43.302
<i>- But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>- And listen to all you say?</i>

00:13:43.539 --> 00:13:47.635
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:13:47.843 --> 00:13:53.679
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:14:09.632 --> 00:14:16.401
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:14:17.306 --> 00:14:23.711
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:14:35.524 --> 00:14:37.515
You may go in now, Maria.

00:14:50.105 --> 00:14:51.732
Come here, my child.

00:14:58.247 --> 00:14:59.612
Now sit down.

00:15:00.549 --> 00:15:04.110
Reverend Mother, I'm sorry.
I couldn't help myself.

00:15:04.386 --> 00:15:07.355
- The hills were beckoning and before...
- Dear.

00:15:07.756 --> 00:15:09.724
I haven't summoned you for apologies.

00:15:09.959 --> 00:15:12.189
Please let me ask for forgiveness.

00:15:12.861 --> 00:15:14.089
If you'll feel better.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.396
Yes, you see,
the sky was so blue today...

00:15:17.633 --> 00:15:21.433
...and everything was so green and
fragrant, I had to be a part of it.

00:15:21.704 --> 00:15:26.198
The Untersberg led me higher like
it wanted me to go through the clouds.

00:15:26.408 --> 00:15:28.433
Suppose darkness had come
and you were lost?

00:15:28.711 --> 00:15:30.941
Mother, I could never be lost
up there.

00:15:31.213 --> 00:15:34.046
That's my mountain.
I was brought up on it.

00:15:34.249 --> 00:15:36.547
It was the mountain that led me
to you.

00:15:37.319 --> 00:15:40.288
When I was a child,
I would come down and climb a tree...

00:15:40.556 --> 00:15:42.319
...and look in your garden.

00:15:42.558 --> 00:15:45.493
I'd see the sisters at work
and hear them sing.

00:15:46.829 --> 00:15:50.458
Which brings me to another
transgression, Reverend Mother.

00:15:50.666 --> 00:15:52.827
I was singing out there today.

00:15:53.502 --> 00:15:57.529
Only in the abbey do we have rules
about postulants singing.

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.765
I can't stop wherever I am.

00:15:59.975 --> 00:16:02.307
Worse, I can't seem to stop
saying things.

00:16:02.578 --> 00:16:04.842
Everything I think and feel.

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:06.513
Some call that "honesty."

00:16:06.782 --> 00:16:09.148
Oh, but it's terrible,
Reverend Mother!

00:16:09.351 --> 00:16:13.253
You know how Sister Berthe makes me
kiss the floor after a disagreement?

00:16:13.622 --> 00:16:17.114
Lately, I kiss the floor
when I see her coming to save time.

00:16:19.795 --> 00:16:20.955
Maria...

00:16:21.964 --> 00:16:24.956
...when you saw us over the wall
and longed to be with us...

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:29.933
...that didn't mean you were prepared
for the way we live here, did it?

00:16:31.273 --> 00:16:33.673
No, Mother, but I pray and I try.

00:16:33.876 --> 00:16:35.605
And I am learning. I really am.

00:16:35.844 --> 00:16:38.506
What is the most important lesson
you have learned here?

00:16:39.181 --> 00:16:42.981
To find out what is the will of God
and do it wholeheartedly.

00:16:45.821 --> 00:16:46.947
Maria...

00:16:48.457 --> 00:16:51.221
...it seems to be God's will
that you leave us.

00:16:51.493 --> 00:16:52.983
- Leave?
- Only for a while.

00:16:53.495 --> 00:16:55.827
No, Mother!
Please don't send me away!

00:16:56.065 --> 00:17:00.331
This is where I belong. It's my home,
my family. It's my life.

00:17:01.003 --> 00:17:04.029
- Are you truly ready for it?
- Yes, I am.

00:17:04.239 --> 00:17:09.142
If you go out into the world for a
time, knowing what we expect of you...

00:17:09.411 --> 00:17:12.141
...you will find out
if you can expect it of yourself.

00:17:12.347 --> 00:17:16.647
I know what you expect, Mother,
and I can do it! I promise I can!

00:17:20.189 --> 00:17:21.417
Yes, Mother.

00:17:23.525 --> 00:17:25.186
If it is God's will.

00:17:27.429 --> 00:17:32.560
There is a family near Salzburg that
needs a governess until September.

00:17:32.768 --> 00:17:34.998
- September?
- For seven children.

00:17:35.671 --> 00:17:36.660
Seven children?!

00:17:36.905 --> 00:17:38.167
Do you like children?

00:17:38.941 --> 00:17:40.772
Well, yes, but seven!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:45.073
I will tell Captain von Trapp
to expect you tomorrow.

00:17:45.614 --> 00:17:47.013
Captain?

00:17:47.716 --> 00:17:52.551
A retired officer of the Imperial
Navy. A fine man and a brave one.

00:17:52.788 --> 00:17:55.518
His wife died,
and he is alone with the children.

00:17:55.724 --> 00:18:00.024
I understand he has had a difficult
time keeping a governess there.

00:18:00.796 --> 00:18:03.094
Why difficult, Reverend Mother?

00:18:04.466 --> 00:18:07.401
The Lord will show you
in His own good time.

00:18:44.273 --> 00:18:46.741
When the Lord closes a door...

00:18:46.942 --> 00:18:49.467
...somewhere He opens a window.

00:18:51.814 --> 00:18:56.808
<i>What will this day be like?</i>

00:18:57.019 --> 00:18:59.249
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:05.761 --> 00:19:09.857
<i>What will my future be?</i>

00:19:10.699 --> 00:19:12.963
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:14.536 --> 00:19:17.630
<i>It could be so exciting</i>

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.934
<i>To be out in the world</i>
<i>To be free</i>

00:19:21.143 --> 00:19:24.203
<i>My heart should be wildly rejoicing</i>

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:30.716
<i>Oh, what's the matter with me?</i>

00:19:31.053 --> 00:19:34.113
<i>I've always longed for adventure</i>

00:19:34.389 --> 00:19:37.950
<i>To do the things I've never dared</i>

00:19:38.193 --> 00:19:41.390
<i>Now here I'm facing adventure</i>

00:19:41.697 --> 00:19:47.795
<i>Then why am I so scared?</i>

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:54.141
<i>A captain with seven children</i>

00:19:54.376 --> 00:19:57.209
<i>What's so fearsome about that?</i>

00:19:59.748 --> 00:20:02.376
<i>I must stop these doubts and worries</i>

00:20:02.651 --> 00:20:05.484
<i>If I don't I just know I'll turn back</i>

00:20:05.754 --> 00:20:08.917
<i>I must dream of the things</i>
<i>I am seeking</i>

00:20:09.992 --> 00:20:14.986
<i>I am seeking the courage I lack</i>

00:20:15.898 --> 00:20:19.732
<i>The courage to serve them</i>
<i>With reliance</i>

00:20:20.002 --> 00:20:22.903
<i>Face my mistakes without defiance</i>

00:20:23.171 --> 00:20:24.866
<i>Show them I'm worthy</i>

00:20:25.107 --> 00:20:27.769
<i>And while I show them</i>

00:20:28.043 --> 00:20:31.843
<i>I'll show me</i>

00:20:32.047 --> 00:20:37.451
<i>So let them bring on</i>
<i>All their problems</i>

00:20:37.686 --> 00:20:40.951
<i>I'll do better than my best</i>

00:20:41.223 --> 00:20:44.283
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>They'll put me to the test</i>

00:20:44.526 --> 00:20:47.962
<i>But I'll make them see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:20:48.196 --> 00:20:51.461
<i>Somehow I will impress them</i>

00:20:51.733 --> 00:20:54.964
<i>I will be firm but kind</i>

00:20:55.237 --> 00:20:58.536
<i>And all those children</i>
<i>Heaven bless them</i>

00:20:58.774 --> 00:21:02.073
<i>They will look up to me</i>
<i>And mind me</i>

00:21:02.311 --> 00:21:05.439
<i>With each step I am more certain</i>

00:21:05.714 --> 00:21:08.979
<i>Everything will turn out fine</i>

00:21:09.217 --> 00:21:12.311
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>The world can all be mine</i>

00:21:12.554 --> 00:21:17.992
<i>They'll have to agree</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:19.561 --> 00:21:22.291
<i>I have confidence in sunshine</i>

00:21:22.564 --> 00:21:25.658
<i>I have confidence in rain</i>

00:21:25.901 --> 00:21:28.768
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>That spring will come again</i>

00:21:29.071 --> 00:21:32.097
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:32.407 --> 00:21:35.467
<i>Strength doesn't lie in numbers</i>

00:21:35.744 --> 00:21:38.770
<i>Strength doesn't lie in wealth</i>

00:21:39.014 --> 00:21:42.347
<i>Strength lies in nights</i>
<i>Of peaceful slumbers</i>

00:21:42.617 --> 00:21:45.484
<i>When you wake up, wake up</i>
<i>It's healthy</i>

00:21:45.787 --> 00:21:48.779
<i>All I trust I leave my heart to</i>

00:21:49.024 --> 00:21:51.925
<i>All I trust becomes my own</i>

00:21:52.127 --> 00:21:56.928
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:11.546 --> 00:22:13.173
Oh, help.

00:22:25.360 --> 00:22:32.027
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:32.834 --> 00:22:37.635
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence...</i>

00:22:37.906 --> 00:22:44.709
<i>...in me</i>

00:22:51.253 --> 00:22:53.653
Hello. Here I am.

00:22:56.491 --> 00:22:58.322
I'm from the convent.
I'm the new governess, captain.

00:22:59.995 --> 00:23:03.226
And I'm the old butler, fräulein.

00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:06.997
Well, how do you do?

00:23:17.512 --> 00:23:21.573
You'll wait here, please.

00:24:47.936 --> 00:24:52.032
In future, remember certain rooms
in this house are not to be disturbed.

00:24:53.208 --> 00:24:54.675
Yes, captain, sir.

00:25:02.617 --> 00:25:07.850
- Why do you stare at me that way?
- You don't look like a sea captain.

00:25:09.057 --> 00:25:12.117
I'm afraid you don't look
very much like a governess.

00:25:12.827 --> 00:25:13.885
- Turn around.
- What?

00:25:14.229 --> 00:25:15.491
Turn.

00:25:18.667 --> 00:25:19.827
Hat off.

00:25:23.038 --> 00:25:25.666
Put on another dress
before meeting the children.

00:25:25.974 --> 00:25:27.532
But I don't have another.

00:25:27.809 --> 00:25:30.676
When we enter the abbey,
our worldly clothes go to the poor.

00:25:30.912 --> 00:25:32.174
What about this one?

00:25:32.380 --> 00:25:33.711
The poor didn't want it.

00:25:35.550 --> 00:25:39.042
There wasn't time to make a new dress.
I can make clothes.

00:25:40.322 --> 00:25:42.586
I'll see that you get some material.

00:25:43.325 --> 00:25:44.849
Today, if possible.

00:25:45.827 --> 00:25:47.590
- Now, fräulein...
- Maria.

00:25:47.829 --> 00:25:50.559
I don't know how much
the abbess told you.

00:25:50.832 --> 00:25:53.392
You are the twelfth governess...

00:25:53.602 --> 00:25:56.070
...to look after my children
since their mother died.

00:25:56.271 --> 00:25:58.501
I trust you will be an improvement
on the last one.

00:25:58.740 --> 00:26:00.571
She stayed only two hours.

00:26:02.277 --> 00:26:04.871
What's wrong with the children, sir?

00:26:06.348 --> 00:26:10.751
Nothing is wrong with the children,
only the governesses.

00:26:11.019 --> 00:26:15.956
They could not maintain discipline,
without which the house cannot be run.

00:26:16.891 --> 00:26:18.688
Drill them in their studies.

00:26:18.927 --> 00:26:22.419
I will not permit them to dream
away their summer holidays.

00:26:22.697 --> 00:26:25.393
Each afternoon,
they march, breathing deeply.

00:26:25.600 --> 00:26:27.261
Bedtime is to be strictly observed.

00:26:27.469 --> 00:26:28.436
When do they play?

00:26:28.637 --> 00:26:32.698
You will see to it that they conduct
themselves with the utmost decorum.

00:26:32.941 --> 00:26:35.876
- I am placing you in command.
- Yes, sir.

00:27:56.524 --> 00:27:57.684
Now...

00:27:58.293 --> 00:28:01.228
...this is your new governess,
Fräulein Maria.

00:28:02.897 --> 00:28:04.888
Give your name at your signal.

00:28:05.200 --> 00:28:09.398
Fräulein, listen carefully. Learn
their signals so you can call them.

00:28:10.705 --> 00:28:12.070
Liesl.

00:28:12.340 --> 00:28:14.069
Friedrich.

00:28:14.342 --> 00:28:15.866
Louisa.

00:28:16.144 --> 00:28:17.406
Kurt.

00:28:17.645 --> 00:28:18.703
Brigitta.

00:28:18.980 --> 00:28:20.208
Marta.

00:28:26.588 --> 00:28:27.919
Gretl.

00:28:32.560 --> 00:28:35.996
Now, let's see how well you listened.

00:28:36.231 --> 00:28:38.597
I won't need to whistle for them,
Reverend Captain.

00:28:38.867 --> 00:28:42.325
I mean, I'll use their names.
Such lovely names.

00:28:42.537 --> 00:28:45.700
Fräulein, this is a large house.
The grounds are extensive.

00:28:45.940 --> 00:28:48.704
And I will not have anyone shouting.

00:28:48.943 --> 00:28:50.672
You will take this, please.
Learn to use it.

00:28:50.879 --> 00:28:52.540
The children will help you.

00:28:54.582 --> 00:28:58.575
Now, when I want you,
this is what you will hear.

00:28:59.454 --> 00:29:01.251
Oh, no, sir. I'm sorry, sir!

00:29:02.123 --> 00:29:03.681
I could never answer to a whistle.

00:29:03.892 --> 00:29:06.520
Whistles are for animals,
not for children.

00:29:06.795 --> 00:29:08.854
And definitely not for me.

00:29:09.097 --> 00:29:11.725
It would be too humiliating.

00:29:12.534 --> 00:29:17.733
Fräulein, were you this much trouble
at the abbey?

00:29:18.039 --> 00:29:19.131
Oh, much more, sir.

00:29:30.251 --> 00:29:31.809
I don't know your signal.

00:29:33.288 --> 00:29:35.916
You may call me "captain."

00:29:48.837 --> 00:29:50.304
At ease.

00:29:53.107 --> 00:29:54.665
Now that there's just us...

00:29:54.943 --> 00:29:59.107
...would you please tell me all your
names again and how old you are.

00:29:59.581 --> 00:30:03.574
I'm Liesl. I'm 16 years old,
and I don't need a governess.

00:30:04.352 --> 00:30:07.412
I'm glad you told me, Liesl.
We'll just be good friends.

00:30:09.591 --> 00:30:13.357
I'm Friedrich. I'm 14.
I'm impossible.

00:30:13.661 --> 00:30:15.322
Really? Who told you that, Friedrich?

00:30:15.597 --> 00:30:19.089
Fräulein Josephine.
Four governesses ago.

00:30:19.534 --> 00:30:21.001
I'm Brigitta.

00:30:22.837 --> 00:30:26.830
You didn't tell me how old you are,
Louisa.

00:30:27.509 --> 00:30:29.773
I'm Brigitta. She's Louisa.

00:30:30.011 --> 00:30:32.775
She's 13 years old, and you're smart.

00:30:33.014 --> 00:30:36.780
I'm 10, and I think your dress
is the ugliest one I ever saw.

00:30:37.118 --> 00:30:39.746
- Brigitta, you shouldn't say that.
- Why not?

00:30:39.954 --> 00:30:42.218
- Don't you think it's ugly?
- Of course.

00:30:42.490 --> 00:30:45.186
But Fräulein Helga's was ugliest.

00:30:45.460 --> 00:30:48.054
I'm Kurt. I'm 11.
I'm incorrigible.

00:30:48.329 --> 00:30:51.457
- Congratulations.
- What's "incorrigible"?

00:30:51.699 --> 00:30:55.567
I think it means you want
to be treated like a boy.

00:30:57.739 --> 00:31:01.038
I'm Marta, and I'm going to be
seven on Tuesday.

00:31:01.309 --> 00:31:02.674
I'd like a pink parasol.

00:31:03.878 --> 00:31:05.402
Pink's my favorite color too.

00:31:07.815 --> 00:31:08.975
Yes, you're Gretl.

00:31:09.884 --> 00:31:11.579
And you're five years old?

00:31:12.020 --> 00:31:14.011
My, you're practically a lady.

00:31:16.524 --> 00:31:19.550
I have to tell you a secret.
I've never been a governess.

00:31:20.995 --> 00:31:23.759
You don't know anything
about being a governess?

00:31:24.032 --> 00:31:25.397
Nothing. I'll need lots of advice.

00:31:26.367 --> 00:31:30.895
The best way to start is to tell
Father to mind his own business.

00:31:31.105 --> 00:31:32.902
Never come to dinner on time.

00:31:33.107 --> 00:31:35.405
Never eat your soup quietly.

00:31:36.077 --> 00:31:38.170
During dessert, always blow your nose.

00:31:38.413 --> 00:31:41.211
Don't you believe a word they say,
Fräulein Maria.

00:31:41.416 --> 00:31:44.783
- Oh, why not?
- Because I like you.

00:31:45.587 --> 00:31:47.578
Children, outside for your walk.

00:31:47.789 --> 00:31:49.689
Father's orders. Hurry up.

00:31:49.891 --> 00:31:51.188
Quick, quick, quick.

00:31:51.426 --> 00:31:54.623
Fräulein Maria, I'm Frau Schmidt,
the housekeeper.

00:31:54.862 --> 00:31:55.920
How do you do.

00:31:56.130 --> 00:31:59.031
I'll show you to your room.
Follow me.

00:32:10.111 --> 00:32:11.874
Poor little dears.

00:32:24.592 --> 00:32:28.961
You're very lucky. With
Fräulein Helga it was a snake.

00:32:42.810 --> 00:32:44.141
Good evening.

00:32:45.580 --> 00:32:49.141
- Good evening, children.
- Good evening, Fräulein Maria.

00:32:56.357 --> 00:32:57.984
Enchanting little ritual.

00:32:58.192 --> 00:33:00.922
Something you learned at the abbey?

00:33:02.130 --> 00:33:04.462
No.

00:33:06.100 --> 00:33:07.362
Rheumatism.

00:33:17.178 --> 00:33:20.341
Excuse me, captain. Haven't we
forgotten to thank the Lord?

00:33:28.556 --> 00:33:31.525
For what we receive,
may the Lord make us truly thankful.

00:33:32.060 --> 00:33:33.994
- Amen.
- Amen.

00:33:38.533 --> 00:33:40.467
I'd like to thank you all...

00:33:40.668 --> 00:33:43.660
...for the precious gift
you left in my pocket today.

00:33:47.175 --> 00:33:48.972
What gift?

00:33:52.080 --> 00:33:54.241
It's a secret between
the children and me.

00:33:54.515 --> 00:33:58.144
Then I suggest you keep it,
and let us eat.

00:33:58.519 --> 00:34:00.487
Knowing how nervous
I must have been...

00:34:00.722 --> 00:34:03.156
...a stranger in a new household...

00:34:03.357 --> 00:34:06.417
...knowing how important it was
for me to feel accepted...

00:34:06.694 --> 00:34:10.892
...it was so kind and thoughtful of
you to make my first moments here...

00:34:11.165 --> 00:34:13.360
...so warm and happy...

00:34:13.568 --> 00:34:15.331
...and pleasant.

00:34:24.579 --> 00:34:26.604
- What is the matter, Marta?
- Nothing.

00:34:39.026 --> 00:34:40.050
Fräulein...

00:34:40.294 --> 00:34:44.128
...is it to be at every meal
or merely at dinnertime...

00:34:44.365 --> 00:34:48.927
...that you intend leading us through
this rare and wonderful new world...

00:34:49.137 --> 00:34:50.798
...of indigestion?

00:34:52.373 --> 00:34:55.240
They're all right, captain.
They're just happy.

00:35:13.995 --> 00:35:16.657
- Rolfe, good evening.
- Good evening, Franz.

00:35:16.931 --> 00:35:19.661
- I trust everything is under control?
- Yes, yes.

00:35:21.302 --> 00:35:23.736
- Are there any developments?
- Perhaps.

00:35:23.938 --> 00:35:26.099
- Is the captain home?
- He's at dinner.

00:35:26.340 --> 00:35:28.672
- With the family?
- Yes.

00:35:28.943 --> 00:35:30.740
Give him this telegram at once.

00:35:31.479 --> 00:35:32.571
Certainly.

00:35:44.258 --> 00:35:45.953
A telegram for you, sir.

00:35:48.796 --> 00:35:50.627
Franz? Who delivered it?

00:35:50.932 --> 00:35:52.957
That young lad Rolfe, of course.

00:35:55.303 --> 00:35:57.032
Father, may I be excused?

00:35:58.005 --> 00:36:02.465
Children, in the morning I shall
be going to Vienna.

00:36:02.777 --> 00:36:05.211
Not again, Father!

00:36:09.116 --> 00:36:11.175
How long will you be gone this time?

00:36:11.819 --> 00:36:13.286
I'm not sure, Gretl.

00:36:13.487 --> 00:36:17.048
- To visit Baroness Schraeder again?
- Mind your own business!

00:36:18.025 --> 00:36:19.959
As a matter of fact, yes, Louisa.

00:36:21.729 --> 00:36:25.563
- Why can't we ever see the baroness?
- Why would she want to see you?

00:36:25.867 --> 00:36:30.736
You are going to see the baroness.
I'm bringing her back with me to visit.

00:36:32.240 --> 00:36:34.037
And Uncle Max.

00:36:34.308 --> 00:36:36.708
Uncle Max!

00:36:52.760 --> 00:36:54.091
Rolfe!

00:36:57.164 --> 00:36:58.222
Oh, Rolfe!

00:37:00.768 --> 00:37:03.703
- No, Liesl. We mustn't!
- Why not, silly?

00:37:03.938 --> 00:37:06.600
- I don't know...
- Isn't this why you're waiting?

00:37:06.841 --> 00:37:08.706
Yes, of course.

00:37:08.910 --> 00:37:11.708
- I've missed you, Liesl.
- You have? How much?

00:37:11.946 --> 00:37:15.780
I even thought of sending a telegram,
so I'd be able to deliver it here.

00:37:16.050 --> 00:37:19.952
Oh, that's a lovely thought!
Why don't you, right now?

00:37:20.221 --> 00:37:24.385
- But I'm here!
- Please, Rolfe. Send me a telegram.

00:37:24.592 --> 00:37:28.050
I'll start it for you.
"Dear Liesl..."

00:37:28.729 --> 00:37:32.358
"Dear Liesl: I'd like to be able
to tell you...

00:37:32.600 --> 00:37:34.795
...how I feel about you. Stop.

00:37:35.036 --> 00:37:39.564
Unfortunately, this wire
is already too expensive.

00:37:39.774 --> 00:37:41.207
Sincerely, Rolfe."

00:37:41.409 --> 00:37:44.173
- "Sincerely"?
- Cordially.

00:37:44.378 --> 00:37:47.040
- "Cordially"?
- Affectionately?

00:37:49.417 --> 00:37:51.442
Will there be any reply?

00:37:52.720 --> 00:37:54.881
"Dear Rolfe: Stop.

00:37:55.890 --> 00:37:58.984
Don't stop! Your Liesl."

00:38:00.728 --> 00:38:04.562
If only we didn't have to wait
for someone to send Father a telegram.

00:38:04.832 --> 00:38:07.232
How do I know when I'll see you again?

00:38:08.135 --> 00:38:09.329
Well, let's see...

00:38:12.340 --> 00:38:14.308
I could come here by mistake.

00:38:15.309 --> 00:38:19.939
With a telegram for Colonel Schneider!
He's here from Berlin staying with...

00:38:20.848 --> 00:38:24.147
No one knows he's here.
Don't tell your father.

00:38:24.418 --> 00:38:27.581
- Why not?
- Your father's so Austrian.

00:38:27.788 --> 00:38:29.085
We're all Austrian.

00:38:29.290 --> 00:38:33.693
Some think we ought to be German, and
they're very mad at those who don't.

00:38:33.928 --> 00:38:35.691
They're getting ready to...

00:38:37.365 --> 00:38:39.799
Let's hope your father
doesn't get into trouble.

00:38:40.101 --> 00:38:45.004
Don't worry. He's a big naval hero.
He was even decorated by the emperor.

00:38:45.206 --> 00:38:48.471
I don't worry about him.
I worry about his daughter.

00:38:49.010 --> 00:38:50.477
Me? Why?

00:38:50.778 --> 00:38:52.336
- Well, you're so...
- What?

00:38:52.780 --> 00:38:54.270
You're such a baby!

00:38:54.715 --> 00:38:57.616
I'm 16.
What's such a baby about that?

00:38:59.854 --> 00:39:03.381
<i>You wait, little girl</i>
<i>On an empty stage</i>

00:39:03.624 --> 00:39:06.991
<i>For fate to turn the light on</i>

00:39:07.628 --> 00:39:10.859
<i>Your life, little girl</i>
<i>Is an empty page</i>

00:39:11.132 --> 00:39:15.193
<i>That men will want to write on</i>

00:39:15.903 --> 00:39:21.398
<i>To write on</i>

00:39:22.343 --> 00:39:26.279
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:26.480 --> 00:39:30.314
<i>Baby, it's time to think</i>

00:39:30.518 --> 00:39:34.147
<i>Better beware</i>
<i>Be canny and careful</i>

00:39:34.388 --> 00:39:38.017
<i>Baby, you're on the brink</i>

00:39:38.359 --> 00:39:42.193
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:42.396 --> 00:39:46.059
<i>Fellows will fall in line</i>

00:39:46.367 --> 00:39:49.700
<i>Eager young lads</i>
<i>And roués and cads</i>

00:39:49.904 --> 00:39:53.840
<i>Will offer you food and wine</i>

00:39:54.108 --> 00:39:57.874
<i>Totally unprepared are you</i>

00:39:58.279 --> 00:40:01.840
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:40:02.416 --> 00:40:06.580
<i>Timid and shy and scared are you</i>

00:40:06.887 --> 00:40:10.379
<i>Of things beyond your ken</i>

00:40:10.591 --> 00:40:14.459
<i>You need someone older and wiser</i>

00:40:14.695 --> 00:40:18.563
<i>Telling you what to do</i>

00:40:18.799 --> 00:40:22.235
<i>I am 17 going on 18</i>

00:40:22.470 --> 00:40:28.431
<i>I'll take care of you</i>

00:41:00.975 --> 00:41:04.308
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:04.512 --> 00:41:07.913
<i>I know that I'm naive</i>

00:41:08.182 --> 00:41:11.413
<i>Fellows I meet</i>
<i>May tell me I'm sweet</i>

00:41:11.652 --> 00:41:15.349
<i>And willingly I believe</i>

00:41:15.823 --> 00:41:18.986
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:19.193 --> 00:41:22.959
<i>Innocent as a rose</i>

00:41:23.164 --> 00:41:26.622
<i>Bachelor dandies</i>
<i>Drinkers of brandies</i>

00:41:26.934 --> 00:41:30.267
<i>What do I know of those?</i>

00:41:30.471 --> 00:41:33.998
<i>Totally unprepared am I</i>

00:41:34.275 --> 00:41:37.767
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:41:38.179 --> 00:41:41.512
<i>Timid and shy and scared am I</i>

00:41:41.782 --> 00:41:45.445
<i>Of things beyond my ken</i>

00:41:45.886 --> 00:41:49.481
<i>I need someone older and wiser</i>

00:41:49.723 --> 00:41:53.022
<i>Telling me what to do</i>

00:41:53.360 --> 00:41:57.057
<i>You are 17 going on 18</i>

00:41:57.298 --> 00:42:02.964
<i>I'll depend on you</i>

00:43:56.016 --> 00:43:57.449
Come in.

00:43:58.485 --> 00:44:00.112
Frau Schmidt.

00:44:02.456 --> 00:44:04.185
For your new dresses.

00:44:04.491 --> 00:44:08.484
- The captain had these sent from town.
- Oh, how lovely!

00:44:08.762 --> 00:44:12.198
These will make the prettiest
clothes I've ever had.

00:44:12.466 --> 00:44:15.958
Do you think he would
get me more material if I asked?

00:44:16.203 --> 00:44:19.832
- How many dresses do you need?
- Not for me, for the children.

00:44:20.107 --> 00:44:22.166
I want to make them some play clothes.

00:44:22.443 --> 00:44:25.970
The von Trapp children don't play.
They march.

00:44:26.480 --> 00:44:28.880
Surely you don't approve of that.

00:44:29.883 --> 00:44:32.283
Ever since the captain
lost his poor wife...

00:44:32.519 --> 00:44:35.215
...he runs this house as if on
one of his ships.

00:44:36.056 --> 00:44:37.455
Whistles, orders.

00:44:37.725 --> 00:44:39.556
No more music, no more laughing.

00:44:39.827 --> 00:44:43.354
Nothing that reminds him of her.
Even the children.

00:44:43.864 --> 00:44:44.956
But that's so wrong.

00:44:45.799 --> 00:44:47.323
Oh, well.

00:44:47.534 --> 00:44:51.197
How do you like your room?
There'll be new drapes at the windows.

00:44:51.472 --> 00:44:52.734
Bu these are fine.

00:44:52.973 --> 00:44:54.634
New ones have been ordered.

00:44:54.842 --> 00:44:58.141
- But I really don't need them.
- Good night, now.

00:44:58.379 --> 00:45:02.406
Frau Schmidt, if I asked
the captain about the material...?

00:45:02.683 --> 00:45:07.143
- He's leaving in the morning.
- Of course. How long will he be gone?

00:45:07.721 --> 00:45:12.317
It depends. The last time he visited
the baroness, he stayed for a month.

00:45:13.494 --> 00:45:18.056
I shouldn't be saying this to you.
I don't know you that well.

00:45:18.332 --> 00:45:21.233
But if you ask me,
the captain's thinking seriously...

00:45:21.435 --> 00:45:23.733
...of marrying her before
summer's over.

00:45:23.937 --> 00:45:27.168
Wonderful! The children will
have a mother again.

00:45:28.609 --> 00:45:29.906
Yes.

00:45:30.177 --> 00:45:31.906
Well, good night.

00:45:32.112 --> 00:45:33.545
Good night.

00:45:51.965 --> 00:45:54.798
Dear Father, now I know
why You sent me here.

00:45:55.035 --> 00:45:57.902
To help these children
prepare for a new mother.

00:45:58.138 --> 00:46:01.437
And I pray this will become
a happy family in Thy sight.

00:46:01.642 --> 00:46:04.770
God bless the captain.
God bless Liesl and Friedrich.

00:46:04.978 --> 00:46:09.142
God bless Louisa, Brigitta,
Marta and little Gretl.

00:46:09.450 --> 00:46:12.283
And I forgot the other boy.
What's his name?

00:46:14.054 --> 00:46:15.885
Well, God bless what's-his-name.

00:46:16.089 --> 00:46:20.082
God bless the Reverend Mother
and Sister Margaretta...

00:46:20.294 --> 00:46:22.091
...and everybody at the abbey.

00:46:22.296 --> 00:46:24.821
And now, dear God, about Liesl.

00:46:25.332 --> 00:46:27.232
Help her know that I'm her friend...

00:46:27.434 --> 00:46:29.994
...and help her tell me
what she's been up to.

00:46:30.737 --> 00:46:31.897
Are you going to tell on me?

00:46:32.139 --> 00:46:35.575
Help me to be understanding
so I may guide her footsteps.

00:46:35.843 --> 00:46:38.471
In the name of the Father,
the Son and the Holy Ghost.

00:46:38.679 --> 00:46:41.671
I was out walking
and somebody locked the doors early.

00:46:41.982 --> 00:46:45.611
I didn't want to wake everybody,
so when I saw your window open...

00:46:47.254 --> 00:46:50.280
You're not going to tell Father,
are you?

00:46:56.363 --> 00:46:57.660
How did you climb up?

00:46:58.165 --> 00:47:01.293
It's how we always got in
to play tricks on the governess.

00:47:01.502 --> 00:47:04.494
Louisa can make it with
a whole jar of spiders in her hand.

00:47:05.506 --> 00:47:07.167
Spiders?

00:47:10.878 --> 00:47:13.506
Were you out walking all by yourself?

00:47:20.988 --> 00:47:24.685
If we wash that dress tonight,
nobody would notice it tomorrow.

00:47:25.359 --> 00:47:27.122
You could put this on.

00:47:28.862 --> 00:47:31.558
Take your dress and put it
to soak in the bathtub.

00:47:31.798 --> 00:47:35.325
Come back here and sit on the bed,
and we'll have a talk.

00:47:36.637 --> 00:47:39.663
I told you today
I didn't need a governess.

00:47:39.873 --> 00:47:41.966
Well, maybe I do.

00:48:12.439 --> 00:48:14.999
Gretl, are you scared?

00:48:18.512 --> 00:48:20.776
You're not frightened
of a storm, are you?

00:48:21.014 --> 00:48:23.278
You just stay right here with me.

00:48:24.451 --> 00:48:28.683
- Where are the others?
- They're asleep. They're not scared.

00:48:33.093 --> 00:48:34.924
Oh, no? Look.

00:48:36.463 --> 00:48:38.431
All right, up here on the bed.

00:48:38.732 --> 00:48:41.428
- Really?
- Well, just this once. Come on.

00:48:42.536 --> 00:48:46.870
- Now we'll wait for the boys.
- You won't see them. Boys are brave.

00:48:52.946 --> 00:48:54.743
You weren't scared, were you?

00:48:55.282 --> 00:48:58.479
Oh, no. We just wanted
to be sure that you weren't.

00:48:59.586 --> 00:49:02.612
- That's very thoughtful of you.
- It wasn't my idea.

00:49:02.923 --> 00:49:04.754
It was Kurt's!

00:49:04.992 --> 00:49:07.586
Kurt! That's the one I left out!
God bless Kurt.

00:49:10.397 --> 00:49:12.160
Why does it do that?

00:49:12.399 --> 00:49:16.233
The lightning talks to the thunder,
and the thunder answers.

00:49:16.470 --> 00:49:18.961
- But lightning must be nasty.
- Not really.

00:49:19.239 --> 00:49:21.503
Why does the thunder get so angry?

00:49:21.775 --> 00:49:23.902
It makes me want to cry.

00:49:25.779 --> 00:49:29.977
Whenever I'm feeling unhappy,
I just try to think of nice things.

00:49:30.183 --> 00:49:32.014
What kind of things?

00:49:32.786 --> 00:49:34.754
Well, let me see. Nice things...

00:49:34.988 --> 00:49:36.080
Daffodils.

00:49:37.357 --> 00:49:38.756
Green meadows.

00:49:39.159 --> 00:49:41.423
Skies full of stars.

00:49:41.628 --> 00:49:44.825
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>and whiskers on kittens</i>

00:49:45.032 --> 00:49:48.160
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:49:48.368 --> 00:49:51.531
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:49:51.805 --> 00:49:55.798
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:49:58.378 --> 00:50:01.176
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:50:01.448 --> 00:50:04.645
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:50:04.885 --> 00:50:07.820
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:50:08.055 --> 00:50:11.889
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:13.160 --> 00:50:15.890
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:50:16.163 --> 00:50:19.360
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:50:19.633 --> 00:50:22.693
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:50:22.969 --> 00:50:26.336
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:26.540 --> 00:50:28.235
<i>When the dog bites</i>

00:50:28.475 --> 00:50:30.136
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:50:30.377 --> 00:50:32.641
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:50:32.879 --> 00:50:36.246
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:50:36.516 --> 00:50:43.354
<i>And then I don't feel so bad</i>

00:50:44.091 --> 00:50:45.752
- Does it work?
- Of course.

00:50:46.059 --> 00:50:47.993
- What do you like?
- Pussy willow!

00:50:48.695 --> 00:50:50.925
- Christmas!
- Bunny rabbits!

00:50:51.164 --> 00:50:52.825
Snakes!

00:50:53.100 --> 00:50:55.227
- Chocolate icing!
- No school!

00:50:55.535 --> 00:50:56.661
Pillow fights!

00:50:56.937 --> 00:50:58.928
- Telegrams!
- Birthday presents!

00:50:59.339 --> 00:51:01.705
- Any presents!
- Ladybugs!

00:51:03.210 --> 00:51:04.541
A good sneeze!

00:51:04.845 --> 00:51:06.574
Gesundheit!

00:51:06.880 --> 00:51:08.108
See what fun it is?

00:51:08.348 --> 00:51:11.283
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

00:51:11.551 --> 00:51:14.418
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:51:14.688 --> 00:51:17.680
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:51:17.924 --> 00:51:20.757
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:24.197 --> 00:51:27.030
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:51:27.267 --> 00:51:30.134
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:51:30.370 --> 00:51:33.305
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:51:33.573 --> 00:51:37.065
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:38.044 --> 00:51:39.534
Together.

00:51:39.813 --> 00:51:42.577
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:51:42.816 --> 00:51:45.717
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:51:45.952 --> 00:51:48.944
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:51:49.222 --> 00:51:52.487
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:52.793 --> 00:51:54.920
<i>When the dog bi...</i>

00:51:55.128 --> 00:51:57.096
Dog bites.

00:52:03.737 --> 00:52:04.965
Hello.

00:52:05.172 --> 00:52:09.336
Fräulein, did I not tell you that
bedtime is to be strictly observed?

00:52:09.643 --> 00:52:12.339
The children were upset
by the storm, so l...

00:52:13.747 --> 00:52:14.736
You did, sir.

00:52:14.948 --> 00:52:19.146
Do you, or do you not, have difficulty
remembering such simple instructions?

00:52:20.453 --> 00:52:22.080
Only during thunderstorms.

00:52:24.591 --> 00:52:26.081
Liesl?

00:52:26.326 --> 00:52:28.521
I don't recall seeing you
after dinner.

00:52:29.129 --> 00:52:30.858
Really? As a matter of fact...

00:52:31.131 --> 00:52:32.359
Yes?

00:52:33.166 --> 00:52:34.326
Well, I was...

00:52:34.601 --> 00:52:36.660
What she would like to say...

00:52:36.870 --> 00:52:39.771
...is that she and I have
been getting acquainted tonight.

00:52:39.973 --> 00:52:44.842
It's too late to go into that. You
heard your father. Go back to bed.

00:52:49.482 --> 00:52:50.881
Fräulein...

00:52:51.184 --> 00:52:55.211
...you have managed to remember
I'm leaving in the morning?

00:52:56.323 --> 00:53:00.851
Is it also possible you remember the
first rule in this house is discipline?

00:53:02.529 --> 00:53:05.020
Then I trust that before I return...

00:53:05.532 --> 00:53:07.295
...you'll have acquired some?

00:53:08.668 --> 00:53:10.033
Captain?

00:53:11.004 --> 00:53:14.906
Could I talk to you about clothes
for the children for when they play?

00:53:15.175 --> 00:53:17.871
- If I could have some material.
- You are many things.

00:53:18.144 --> 00:53:20.305
Not the least of which is repetitious.

00:53:20.513 --> 00:53:22.674
- But they're children!
- Yes.

00:53:22.916 --> 00:53:24.679
And I'm their father.

00:53:25.252 --> 00:53:26.480
Good night.

00:53:50.744 --> 00:53:56.580
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:54:08.094 --> 00:54:11.621
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:54:11.865 --> 00:54:14.356
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:54:14.601 --> 00:54:17.900
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:54:18.104 --> 00:54:20.231
<i>And then I don't feel...</i>

00:54:20.473 --> 00:54:27.402
<i>...so bad</i>

00:54:51.404 --> 00:54:54.100
Children, over here. See!

00:54:57.744 --> 00:54:59.109
Come on.

00:56:22.162 --> 00:56:23.390
Fräulein Maria?

00:56:23.663 --> 00:56:25.563
Can we do this every day?

00:56:25.865 --> 00:56:29.062
- Don't you think you'd get tired of it?
- I suppose so.

00:56:29.402 --> 00:56:30.664
Every other day?

00:56:30.870 --> 00:56:35.500
I haven't had so much fun since we put
glue on Fräulein Josephine's toothbrush.

00:56:35.708 --> 00:56:39.610
I can't understand how children
as nice as you can play such tricks.

00:56:39.879 --> 00:56:41.710
- It's easy.
- But why do it?

00:56:41.915 --> 00:56:44.349
How else can we get
Father's attention?

00:56:45.118 --> 00:56:46.710
Oh, I see.

00:56:48.054 --> 00:56:50.249
We'll have to think about that one.

00:56:52.425 --> 00:56:54.052
All right, over here.

00:56:54.260 --> 00:56:55.693
What are we going to do?

00:56:55.929 --> 00:56:57.897
Think of a song for the baroness.

00:56:58.131 --> 00:57:00.099
Father doesn't like us to sing.

00:57:00.366 --> 00:57:03.927
Perhaps we can change his mind.
Now, what songs do you know?

00:57:04.204 --> 00:57:06.365
We don't know any songs.

00:57:06.606 --> 00:57:09.268
- Not any?
- We don't even know how to sing.

00:57:10.944 --> 00:57:13.105
Let's not lose time. You must learn.

00:57:13.379 --> 00:57:15.108
But how?

00:57:19.419 --> 00:57:23.378
<i>Let's start at the very beginning</i>

00:57:23.590 --> 00:57:26.957
<i>A very good place to start</i>

00:57:27.160 --> 00:57:29.094
<i>When you read you begin with</i>

00:57:29.329 --> 00:57:30.557
<i>A, B, C</i>

00:57:30.763 --> 00:57:35.097
<i>When you sing, you begin with</i>
<i>Do-Re-Mi</i>

00:57:35.335 --> 00:57:36.962
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:37.237 --> 00:57:38.568
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:38.805 --> 00:57:42.639
<i>The first three notes</i>
<i>Just happen to be</i>

00:57:42.909 --> 00:57:44.672
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:44.911 --> 00:57:46.173
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:46.412 --> 00:57:50.348
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti</i>

00:57:51.017 --> 00:57:53.451
Let's see if I can make it easier.

00:57:56.856 --> 00:58:00.519
<i>"Doe," a deer</i>
<i>A female deer</i>

00:58:00.760 --> 00:58:04.321
<i>"Ray," a drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:04.597 --> 00:58:08.363
<i>"Me," a name I call myself</i>

00:58:08.635 --> 00:58:12.332
<i>"Far," a long long way to run</i>

00:58:12.605 --> 00:58:16.371
<i>"Sew," a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:16.676 --> 00:58:20.510
<i>"La," a note to follow sew</i>

00:58:20.780 --> 00:58:23.715
<i>"Tea," a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:24.184 --> 00:58:28.280
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:58:28.788 --> 00:58:32.349
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:32.625 --> 00:58:35.822
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:36.062 --> 00:58:39.361
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

00:58:39.632 --> 00:58:42.726
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

00:58:43.236 --> 00:58:46.694
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:46.906 --> 00:58:50.239
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

00:58:50.677 --> 00:58:53.544
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:53.813 --> 00:58:56.077
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

00:58:56.316 --> 00:58:59.752
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:59:00.019 --> 00:59:03.079
<i>Ray, a drop of golden sun</i>

00:59:03.556 --> 00:59:06.753
<i>Me, a name I call myself</i>

00:59:07.026 --> 00:59:10.086
<i>Far, a long long way to run</i>

00:59:10.363 --> 00:59:13.594
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:59:13.900 --> 00:59:17.267
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

00:59:17.537 --> 00:59:20.165
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:59:20.373 --> 00:59:24.434
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:59:24.844 --> 00:59:27.938
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do, so-do</i>

00:59:28.381 --> 00:59:32.943
Do-re-mi-fa-so and so on are only
the tools we use to build a song.

00:59:33.219 --> 00:59:36.450
Once you have them in your head
you can sing different tunes...

00:59:36.723 --> 00:59:38.850
...by mixing them up. Like this:

00:59:40.093 --> 00:59:45.588
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:45.798 --> 00:59:46.890
Can you do that?

00:59:47.100 --> 00:59:52.595
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:52.805 --> 00:59:58.471
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

00:59:58.778 --> 01:00:04.080
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:04.284 --> 01:00:06.047
Now, put it all together.

01:00:06.252 --> 01:00:12.885
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:00:13.126 --> 01:00:19.087
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:19.666 --> 01:00:22.260
- Good.
- But it doesn't mean anything.

01:00:22.502 --> 01:00:25.471
So we put in words.
One word for every note.

01:00:25.738 --> 01:00:27.000
Like this:

01:00:27.240 --> 01:00:33.804
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:34.080 --> 01:00:39.677
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:39.952 --> 01:00:40.919
Together!

01:00:41.120 --> 01:00:47.821
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:48.027 --> 01:00:54.694
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:55.101 --> 01:00:58.468
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

01:00:58.738 --> 01:01:01.935
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

01:01:02.208 --> 01:01:05.439
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

01:01:05.645 --> 01:01:08.705
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

01:01:08.948 --> 01:01:12.315
<i>- Sew</i>
<i>- A needle pulling thread</i>

01:01:12.618 --> 01:01:15.883
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

01:01:16.089 --> 01:01:19.081
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:01:19.292 --> 01:01:23.160
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

01:01:40.747 --> 01:01:47.016
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:01:47.587 --> 01:01:54.083
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:01:54.660 --> 01:01:57.823
<i>Doe</i>
<i>A deer, a female deer</i>

01:01:58.097 --> 01:02:01.624
<i>Ray</i>
<i>A drop of golden sun</i>

01:02:01.834 --> 01:02:05.292
<i>Me</i>
<i>A name I call myself</i>

01:02:05.538 --> 01:02:08.701
<i>Far</i>
<i>A long long way to run</i>

01:02:08.975 --> 01:02:12.138
<i>Sew</i>
<i>A needle pulling thread</i>

01:02:12.345 --> 01:02:15.542
<i>La</i>
<i>A note to follow sew</i>

01:02:16.149 --> 01:02:18.777
<i>Tea</i>
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:02:19.018 --> 01:02:22.977
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

01:02:23.189 --> 01:02:30.027
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:02:30.296 --> 01:02:34.790
<i>So-do-la-fa-ti</i>

01:02:35.034 --> 01:02:36.661
<i>La-so</i>

01:02:40.206 --> 01:02:46.008
<i>Ti-do</i>

01:02:46.212 --> 01:02:47.702
<i>So-do</i>

01:03:01.160 --> 01:03:04.254
The mountains are magnificent,
really magnificent.

01:03:04.497 --> 01:03:07.159
- I had them put up just for you.
- Oh?

01:03:07.433 --> 01:03:09.594
Even if it's to a height
of 10,000 feet...

01:03:09.869 --> 01:03:13.396
...Georg always believes in
"rising to the occasion."

01:03:13.673 --> 01:03:15.937
Improve the jokes
or I'll disinvite you.

01:03:16.542 --> 01:03:19.102
You didn't invite me.
I invited myself.

01:03:19.378 --> 01:03:21.903
- Naturally.
- You needed a chaperone...

01:03:22.181 --> 01:03:24.911
...and I needed a place
where the cuisine is superb...

01:03:25.184 --> 01:03:27.778
...the wine cellar unexcelled...

01:03:28.087 --> 01:03:30.681
...and the price perfect.

01:03:31.057 --> 01:03:32.888
Max, you are outrageous.

01:03:33.125 --> 01:03:37.118
Not at all.
I'm a very charming sponge.

01:03:39.765 --> 01:03:40.891
Listen.

01:03:43.236 --> 01:03:45.466
That's the Klopmann Monastery Choir.

01:03:48.474 --> 01:03:50.101
They're good.

01:03:51.143 --> 01:03:52.770
Very good.

01:03:53.579 --> 01:03:56.241
I must explore this area
in the next few days.

01:03:56.449 --> 01:03:59.907
Somewhere, a hungry singing group
is waiting for Max Detweiler...

01:04:00.152 --> 01:04:04.452
...to pluck it out and make it famous
at the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:04:04.657 --> 01:04:07.956
- They get fame, you get money.
- It's unfair, I admit it.

01:04:08.227 --> 01:04:12.596
But someday that'll be changed.
I shall get the fame too.

01:04:19.639 --> 01:04:21.800
Good heavens, what's this?

01:04:23.242 --> 01:04:25.574
It's nothing.
Just some local urchins.

01:04:40.793 --> 01:04:44.695
This really is exciting for me, Georg.
Being here with you.

01:04:45.531 --> 01:04:48.091
Trees, lakes,
you've seen them before.

01:04:48.367 --> 01:04:50.961
That is not what I mean,
and you know it.

01:04:51.203 --> 01:04:55.162
- You mean me? I'm exciting?
- Is that so impossible?

01:04:55.441 --> 01:04:58.467
No, just highly improbable.

01:04:58.711 --> 01:05:02.875
- There you go, running yourself down.
- Well, I'm a dangerous driver.

01:05:06.652 --> 01:05:10.349
You're much less of a riddle
when I see you here, Georg.

01:05:10.556 --> 01:05:13.389
- In my natural habitat?
- Yes, exactly.

01:05:13.693 --> 01:05:15.820
Are you saying that I'm more
at home...

01:05:16.062 --> 01:05:20.055
...among the birds and the flowers
and the wind that moves...

01:05:20.333 --> 01:05:22.494
...through the trees
like a restless sea?

01:05:22.735 --> 01:05:24.327
How poetic.

01:05:24.537 --> 01:05:26.402
Yes, it was rather, wasn't it?

01:05:27.540 --> 01:05:32.671
More at home here than in Vienna
in all your glittering salons...

01:05:32.878 --> 01:05:37.247
...gossiping gaily with bores I
detest, soaking myself in champagne...

01:05:37.550 --> 01:05:41.247
...stumbling about to waltzes
by Strausses I can't even remember?

01:05:41.554 --> 01:05:43.681
- Is that what you're saying?
- Yes.

01:05:43.923 --> 01:05:46.221
Now whatever gave you that idea?

01:05:49.595 --> 01:05:53.497
Oh, I do like it here, Georg.
It's so lovely and peaceful.

01:05:53.833 --> 01:05:55.767
How can you leave it so often?

01:05:56.035 --> 01:05:58.868
Oh, pretending to be madly active,
I suppose.

01:05:59.105 --> 01:06:02.370
Activity suggests a life
filled with purpose.

01:06:03.109 --> 01:06:05.373
Could it be running away
from memories?

01:06:08.581 --> 01:06:12.517
Or perhaps just searching
for a reason to stay.

01:06:13.185 --> 01:06:16.677
I hope that's why you've been
coming to Vienna so often.

01:06:17.356 --> 01:06:21.690
- Were there other distractions?
- I'd hardly call you a distraction.

01:06:21.927 --> 01:06:24.589
Well, what would you call me, Georg?

01:06:26.866 --> 01:06:28.128
Lovely...

01:06:29.135 --> 01:06:31.763
...charming, witty, graceful,
the perfect hostess...

01:06:31.971 --> 01:06:34.804
...and, you're going to hate me
for this...

01:06:35.241 --> 01:06:37.300
...in a way, my savior.

01:06:37.576 --> 01:06:39.407
Oh, how unromantic.

01:06:39.612 --> 01:06:41.944
I'd be an ungrateful wretch
if I didn't say...

01:06:42.214 --> 01:06:45.445
...that you brought some meaning back
into my life.

01:06:47.286 --> 01:06:50.050
I am amusing, I suppose.

01:06:50.289 --> 01:06:55.056
I have the finest couturier in Vienna
and a glittering circle of friends.

01:06:55.261 --> 01:06:58.389
- I do give some rather gay parties.
- Oh, yes.

01:06:58.631 --> 01:07:00.462
But take all that away...

01:07:00.666 --> 01:07:05.103
...and you have just wealthy,
unattached little me...

01:07:05.771 --> 01:07:08.171
...searching, just like you.

01:07:13.279 --> 01:07:14.974
More strudel, Herr Detweiler?

01:07:15.247 --> 01:07:16.771
- How many have I had?
- Two.

01:07:17.016 --> 01:07:18.950
Make it an uneven three.

01:07:22.254 --> 01:07:25.280
Still eating, Max?
Must be unhappy.

01:07:25.491 --> 01:07:29.450
That mixed quartet I've been trying
to steal away from Sol Hurok...

01:07:29.695 --> 01:07:32.357
- What happened?
...Sascha Petrie stole them first.

01:07:32.598 --> 01:07:33.860
I hate thieves.

01:07:34.133 --> 01:07:37.432
Max, you really must try
and learn to love yourself.

01:07:37.670 --> 01:07:40.002
I had to call Paris, Rome
and Stockholm.

01:07:40.272 --> 01:07:43.833
- On Georg's telephone, of course.
- How else could I afford it?

01:07:44.310 --> 01:07:49.441
I like rich people, the way they live
and how I live when I'm with them.

01:07:49.782 --> 01:07:51.773
I wonder where the children are.

01:07:52.184 --> 01:07:54.675
They must have heard
I was coming and hid.

01:07:54.954 --> 01:07:57.445
I was hoping they'd be here
to welcome you.

01:07:57.690 --> 01:08:02.184
Max, do step out of character for
a moment and try and be charming.

01:08:11.237 --> 01:08:12.636
Well?

01:08:13.539 --> 01:08:14.733
Well what?

01:08:14.974 --> 01:08:17.875
Have you made up his mind?
Do I hear wedding bells?

01:08:18.144 --> 01:08:20.135
- Pealing madly.
- Marvelous.

01:08:20.379 --> 01:08:23.143
- Not necessarily for me.
- What kind of talk's that?

01:08:23.349 --> 01:08:24.907
None-of-your-business talk.

01:08:25.217 --> 01:08:27.651
I'm terribly fond of him,
so don't toy with us.

01:08:27.920 --> 01:08:31.515
But I'm a child. I like toys.
So tell me everything.

01:08:31.824 --> 01:08:36.887
Come on. Tell me every teensy-weensy,
intimate, disgusting detail.

01:08:38.364 --> 01:08:42.494
Well, let's just say I have a feeling
I may be here on approval.

01:08:42.735 --> 01:08:45.761
- I approve of that. How can you miss?
- Far too easily.

01:08:46.038 --> 01:08:49.269
If I know you, darling,
and I do, you will find a way.

01:08:49.542 --> 01:08:52.033
- He's no ordinary man.
- No, he's rich.

01:08:52.278 --> 01:08:54.542
His wife's death gave him
a great heartache.

01:08:54.747 --> 01:08:57.875
And your husband's death
gave you a great fortune.

01:08:58.083 --> 01:09:00.051
Oh, Max, you really are a beast.

01:09:00.252 --> 01:09:04.279
You and Georg are like family.
That's why I want to see you married.

01:09:04.523 --> 01:09:08.084
We must keep all that lovely money
in the family.

01:09:24.376 --> 01:09:27.311
- What are you doing there?
- Oh, Captain von Trapp.

01:09:27.580 --> 01:09:29.605
I was just looking for...

01:09:30.482 --> 01:09:33.315
I didn't see, I mean,
I didn't know you were...

01:09:33.919 --> 01:09:35.614
Heil Hitler!

01:09:36.322 --> 01:09:37.812
Who are you?

01:09:38.090 --> 01:09:40.320
I have a telegram for Herr Detweiler.

01:09:40.593 --> 01:09:43.323
- I am Herr Detweiler.
- Yes, sir.

01:09:48.400 --> 01:09:50.994
You've delivered your telegram.
Now get out.

01:09:57.776 --> 01:10:01.177
- Georg, he's just a boy.
- Yes, and I'm just an Austrian.

01:10:01.413 --> 01:10:04.177
Things will happen.
Make sure they don't happen to you.

01:10:04.483 --> 01:10:07.145
Max! Don't you ever say that again.

01:10:07.419 --> 01:10:09.614
I have no political convictions.

01:10:09.855 --> 01:10:12.790
- Can I help it if other people do?
- You can help it.

01:10:13.926 --> 01:10:16.087
You must help it.

01:10:26.372 --> 01:10:27.964
Hello?

01:10:30.609 --> 01:10:33.373
You're far away. Where are you?

01:10:33.679 --> 01:10:37.547
In a world that's disappearing,
I'm afraid.

01:10:38.384 --> 01:10:41.979
Is there any way I could bring you
back to the world I'm in?

01:11:07.913 --> 01:11:10.404
- Father! Father!
- There's your father!

01:11:11.216 --> 01:11:13.844
Oh, captain, you're home!

01:11:22.227 --> 01:11:24.889
Come out of that water at once!

01:11:34.006 --> 01:11:36.201
Oh, you must be Baroness Schraeder.

01:11:41.513 --> 01:11:44.505
I'm soaked to the skin!

01:11:56.462 --> 01:11:57.861
Straight line!

01:12:12.544 --> 01:12:14.944
This is Baroness Schraeder.

01:12:17.549 --> 01:12:19.312
And these...

01:12:19.551 --> 01:12:21.143
...are my children.

01:12:22.254 --> 01:12:23.744
How do you do?

01:12:24.823 --> 01:12:29.556
Go inside, dry off, clean up, change
your clothes and report back here!

01:12:34.566 --> 01:12:36.659
Fräulein, you will stay here, please!

01:12:38.404 --> 01:12:41.965
I think I'd better go see
what Max is up to.

01:12:52.184 --> 01:12:53.947
Now, fräulein...

01:12:55.854 --> 01:12:57.913
...I want a truthful answer.

01:12:58.323 --> 01:12:59.790
Yes, captain.

01:13:00.092 --> 01:13:04.153
Is it possible,
or could I have just imagined it?

01:13:05.664 --> 01:13:10.158
Have my children, by any chance,
been climbing trees today?

01:13:10.636 --> 01:13:11.796
Yes, captain.

01:13:12.871 --> 01:13:14.202
I see.

01:13:14.773 --> 01:13:19.267
And where, may I ask,
did they get these...

01:13:19.545 --> 01:13:21.604
- Play clothes.
- Is that what they are?

01:13:21.814 --> 01:13:25.215
I made them from the drapes
that used to hang in my bedroom.

01:13:26.018 --> 01:13:28.145
- Drapes?
- They have plenty of wear left.

01:13:28.353 --> 01:13:30.287
We've been everywhere in them.

01:13:30.522 --> 01:13:34.982
Are you telling me that my children
have been roaming about Salzburg...

01:13:35.194 --> 01:13:38.561
...dressed up in nothing
but some old drapes?

01:13:38.797 --> 01:13:40.458
And having a marvelous time!

01:13:40.666 --> 01:13:43.897
- They have uniforms.
- Forgive me, straitjackets.

01:13:44.136 --> 01:13:46.900
They can't be children
if they worry about clothes...

01:13:47.172 --> 01:13:48.298
They don't complain.

01:13:48.540 --> 01:13:51.236
They don't dare.
They love you too much and fear...

01:13:51.477 --> 01:13:53.035
Don't discuss my children.

01:13:53.245 --> 01:13:55.179
You've got to hear, you're
never home...

01:13:55.380 --> 01:13:56.904
I don't want to hear more!

01:13:57.149 --> 01:13:59.640
I know you don't, but you've got to!

01:14:00.419 --> 01:14:02.580
- Liesl's not a child.
- Not one word...

01:14:02.855 --> 01:14:05.722
Soon she'll be a woman
and you won't even know her.

01:14:05.991 --> 01:14:09.051
Friedrich wants to be a man
but you're not here to show...

01:14:09.328 --> 01:14:10.659
Don't you dare tell me...

01:14:10.896 --> 01:14:14.161
Brigitta could tell you about him.
She notices everything.

01:14:14.399 --> 01:14:17.527
Kurt acts tough to hide the pain
when you ignore him...

01:14:17.736 --> 01:14:19.260
...the way you do all of them.

01:14:19.538 --> 01:14:21.938
Louisa, I don't know about yet.

01:14:22.207 --> 01:14:25.404
The little ones just want love.
Please, love them all.

01:14:25.677 --> 01:14:27.201
I don't care to hear more.

01:14:27.446 --> 01:14:31.542
- I am not finished yet, captain!
- Oh, yes, you are, captain!

01:14:33.085 --> 01:14:34.245
Fräulein.

01:14:35.554 --> 01:14:39.684
Now, you will pack
your things this minute...

01:14:39.892 --> 01:14:42.383
...and return to the abbey.

01:14:45.030 --> 01:14:46.361
What's that?

01:14:48.100 --> 01:14:49.124
It's singing.

01:14:49.768 --> 01:14:52.566
Yes, I realize it's singing.
But who is singing?

01:14:53.539 --> 01:14:55.097
The children.

01:14:57.976 --> 01:14:59.307
The children?

01:14:59.878 --> 01:15:02.608
I taught them something to sing
for the baroness.

01:15:08.253 --> 01:15:14.283
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

01:15:14.560 --> 01:15:17.120
<i>Every song that it hears</i>

01:15:17.396 --> 01:15:22.834
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

01:15:23.101 --> 01:15:26.229
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

01:15:26.471 --> 01:15:27.904
<i>To the trees</i>

01:15:28.140 --> 01:15:33.077
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

01:15:33.278 --> 01:15:37.908
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

01:15:38.183 --> 01:15:42.085
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

01:15:42.354 --> 01:15:45.289
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

01:15:45.591 --> 01:15:46.956
<i>On its way</i>

01:15:47.192 --> 01:15:51.629
<i>To sing through the night</i>

01:15:51.830 --> 01:15:57.496
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

01:15:57.769 --> 01:16:02.263
<i>I go to the hills</i>

01:16:02.474 --> 01:16:08.709
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

01:16:08.981 --> 01:16:12.678
<i>I know I will hear</i>

01:16:12.951 --> 01:16:18.719
<i>What I've heard before</i>

01:16:19.558 --> 01:16:23.790
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

01:16:24.029 --> 01:16:30.992
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:16:31.870 --> 01:16:37.069
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

01:16:37.309 --> 01:16:45.409
<i>...once more</i>

01:17:18.684 --> 01:17:20.447
Edelweiss!

01:17:24.423 --> 01:17:27.586
You never told me how enchanting
your children are.

01:17:36.201 --> 01:17:37.759
Don't go away.

01:17:42.874 --> 01:17:44.273
Fräulein.

01:17:47.612 --> 01:17:48.806
I...

01:17:50.282 --> 01:17:53.080
...behaved badly. I apologize.

01:17:54.820 --> 01:17:58.415
I'm far too outspoken.
It's one of my worst faults.

01:17:58.824 --> 01:18:00.291
You were right.

01:18:02.761 --> 01:18:04.661
I don't know my children.

01:18:05.964 --> 01:18:10.094
There's still time, captain.
They want so much to be close to you.

01:18:10.435 --> 01:18:14.303
And you brought music back
into the house.

01:18:15.640 --> 01:18:17.073
I'd forgotten.

01:18:19.811 --> 01:18:21.142
Fräulein.

01:18:23.648 --> 01:18:24.910
I want you to stay.

01:18:28.920 --> 01:18:31.650
I ask you to stay.

01:18:33.492 --> 01:18:36.984
- If I could be of any help.
- You have already.

01:18:37.596 --> 01:18:38.654
More than you know.

01:18:58.383 --> 01:18:59.714
Marta.

01:19:00.452 --> 01:19:01.680
Curtain!

01:19:04.356 --> 01:19:07.689
<i>High on a hill was a lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:09.194 --> 01:19:12.459
<i>Loud was the voice</i>
<i>Of the lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:13.965 --> 01:19:17.230
<i>Folks in a town</i>
<i>That was quite remote heard</i>

01:19:18.804 --> 01:19:22.035
<i>Lusty and clear</i>
<i>From the goatherd's throat heard</i>

01:19:33.552 --> 01:19:36.419
Marta. Marta!

01:19:38.824 --> 01:19:40.815
Gretl, the prince!

01:19:42.561 --> 01:19:46.019
<i>A prince on the bridge</i>
<i>Of a castle moat heard</i>

01:19:47.499 --> 01:19:49.831
<i>Men on a road</i>
<i>With a load to tote heard</i>

01:19:52.337 --> 01:19:55.602
<i>Men in the midst</i>
<i>Of a table d'hôte heard</i>

01:19:56.942 --> 01:20:00.207
<i>Men drinking beer</i>
<i>With the foam afloat heard</i>

01:20:11.289 --> 01:20:14.417
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:20:16.061 --> 01:20:19.394
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:20:20.565 --> 01:20:23.966
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:20:25.470 --> 01:20:28.769
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:15.353 --> 01:21:18.618
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:21:20.158 --> 01:21:23.423
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:21:24.763 --> 01:21:28.199
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:21:29.668 --> 01:21:32.796
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:34.506 --> 01:21:36.133
<i>Happy are they</i>

01:21:39.110 --> 01:21:42.375
<i>Soon the duet will become a trio</i>

01:22:06.871 --> 01:22:08.463
- Bravo!
- Bravo!

01:22:08.673 --> 01:22:10.163
Very good!

01:22:11.977 --> 01:22:13.877
Wonderful!

01:22:14.479 --> 01:22:17.642
- Can we keep the puppets, Uncle Max?
- Yes, can we?

01:22:17.849 --> 01:22:19.874
Of course you may, my darlings.

01:22:20.085 --> 01:22:24.317
Why else did I tell Professor Kohner
to send the bill to your father?

01:22:28.059 --> 01:22:29.720
Well done, fräulein.

01:22:32.230 --> 01:22:34.198
I really am very much impressed.

01:22:34.399 --> 01:22:36.390
They're your children, captain.

01:22:43.608 --> 01:22:45.906
My dear, is there anything
you can't do?

01:22:46.177 --> 01:22:48.509
Well, I'm not sure
I'll make a good nun.

01:22:48.747 --> 01:22:51.841
If you have any problems,
I'd be happy to help you.

01:22:54.953 --> 01:22:56.386
Attention, everyone!

01:22:56.588 --> 01:23:00.046
I have an announcement to make.
Surprise! Surprise!

01:23:00.291 --> 01:23:02.589
Today, after a long
and desperate search...

01:23:02.861 --> 01:23:07.855
...I have found a most exciting
entry for the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:23:08.066 --> 01:23:09.897
Congratulations, Max.

01:23:10.135 --> 01:23:13.104
And who will you
be exploiting this time?

01:23:14.906 --> 01:23:18.103
- The Saint Ignatius Choir?
- Guess again.

01:23:18.810 --> 01:23:22.746
Well, let me see now.
The Klopmann Choir?

01:23:22.981 --> 01:23:25.381
- No, no, no, no.
- No, no?

01:23:25.583 --> 01:23:26.777
Tell us.

01:23:26.985 --> 01:23:30.443
A singing group all in one family.
You'll never guess, Georg.

01:23:30.722 --> 01:23:33.623
What a charming idea!

01:23:33.825 --> 01:23:35.622
Whose family?

01:23:36.494 --> 01:23:38.121
Yours.

01:23:38.329 --> 01:23:40.661
They'll be the talk of the festival.

01:23:43.501 --> 01:23:46.493
- Well, now, what's so funny?
- You are, Max.

01:23:46.771 --> 01:23:49.899
You're expensive, but very funny.

01:23:50.642 --> 01:23:52.974
- They'll be a sensation!
- No, Max.

01:23:53.244 --> 01:23:55.439
It's a wonderful idea.
Fresh, original.

01:23:55.647 --> 01:24:00.448
Max! My children
do not sing in public.

01:24:01.119 --> 01:24:03.087
You can't blame me for trying.

01:24:03.288 --> 01:24:06.280
Children, who shall we hear
from next?

01:24:09.094 --> 01:24:10.254
Who?

01:24:16.434 --> 01:24:17.628
Yes.

01:24:20.505 --> 01:24:22.439
The vote is unanimous.

01:24:23.274 --> 01:24:24.832
You, captain.

01:24:25.110 --> 01:24:26.304
Me?

01:24:27.145 --> 01:24:29.443
- I don't understand.
- Please.

01:24:35.653 --> 01:24:37.780
No, no, no, no.

01:24:38.056 --> 01:24:40.115
I'm told that you were quite good.

01:24:40.325 --> 01:24:43.624
- That was a very, very long time ago.
- I remember, Father.

01:24:43.862 --> 01:24:46.729
- Play us something we know.
- Oh, please, Father.

01:24:49.667 --> 01:24:50.725
Well...

01:25:00.979 --> 01:25:03.140
- Why didn't you tell me?
- What?

01:25:03.414 --> 01:25:05.712
To bring along my harmonica.

01:25:08.052 --> 01:25:10.179
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:11.756 --> 01:25:14.054
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:15.160 --> 01:25:21.360
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:25:21.599 --> 01:25:24.659
<i>Small and white</i>

01:25:25.503 --> 01:25:28.870
<i>Clean and bright</i>

01:25:29.073 --> 01:25:31.906
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:25:32.110 --> 01:25:35.944
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:25:36.214 --> 01:25:38.512
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:25:38.783 --> 01:25:42.913
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:25:43.121 --> 01:25:49.458
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:25:50.428 --> 01:25:54.125
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:54.365 --> 01:25:56.959
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:57.635 --> 01:26:04.905
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:26:09.280 --> 01:26:12.477
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:12.784 --> 01:26:16.276
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:16.487 --> 01:26:22.892
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:26:23.127 --> 01:26:26.654
<i>- Small and white</i>
<i>- Small and white</i>

01:26:26.931 --> 01:26:30.389
<i>- Clean and bright</i>
<i>- Clean and bright</i>

01:26:30.602 --> 01:26:33.093
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:26:33.338 --> 01:26:36.967
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:26:37.442 --> 01:26:39.569
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:26:39.777 --> 01:26:43.941
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:26:44.182 --> 01:26:51.247
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:26:51.489 --> 01:26:55.118
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:55.360 --> 01:26:58.022
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:58.630 --> 01:27:08.528
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:27:17.815 --> 01:27:21.478
Anytime you say the word, Georg,
you can be part of my new act:

01:27:21.686 --> 01:27:24.177
The von Trapp Family Singers.

01:27:25.290 --> 01:27:27.781
I have a wonderful idea, Georg.

01:27:28.026 --> 01:27:30.494
Let's really fill this house
with music.

01:27:30.728 --> 01:27:33.697
You must give a grand
and glorious party for me.

01:27:33.965 --> 01:27:36.661
- A party?
- Yes, Father, please!

01:27:36.868 --> 01:27:39.234
It's high time
I met all your friends...

01:27:39.537 --> 01:27:42.028
...and they met me.
Don't you agree?

01:27:42.307 --> 01:27:44.537
- I see what you mean.
- Oh, please!

01:27:44.809 --> 01:27:47.972
Children, it's bedtime.
Come now, say good night.

01:27:48.913 --> 01:27:50.210
Good night, Father.

01:27:50.415 --> 01:27:53.248
- Good night.
- Good night, Baroness Schraeder.

01:27:53.484 --> 01:27:55.042
Good night, Father.

01:27:58.022 --> 01:27:59.853
Good night, Uncle Max.

01:28:01.759 --> 01:28:04.922
It'll be my first party, Father!

01:28:37.462 --> 01:28:40.090
- Captain.
- Herr Zeller. Baroness Schraeder.

01:28:40.298 --> 01:28:43.426
- Good evening, Herr Zeller.
- Baroness.

01:28:44.736 --> 01:28:47.204
How do you do? Good evening.

01:29:07.825 --> 01:29:11.261
Did you notice the obvious
display of the Austrian flag?

01:29:18.336 --> 01:29:20.133
The women look so beautiful.

01:29:20.405 --> 01:29:21.736
I think they look ugly.

01:29:22.006 --> 01:29:23.837
You're just scared of them.

01:29:24.075 --> 01:29:26.305
Silly, only grown-up men fear women.

01:29:26.911 --> 01:29:30.472
- I think the men look beautiful.
- How would you know?

01:29:47.765 --> 01:29:49.790
Liesl, who are you dancing with?

01:29:50.001 --> 01:29:51.628
Nobody.

01:29:52.437 --> 01:29:54.337
Oh, yes, you are.

01:29:56.808 --> 01:29:58.298
May I have this dance?

01:29:58.509 --> 01:30:01.000
I'd be delighted, young man.

01:30:07.785 --> 01:30:10.447
Why didn't you tell me
you could dance?

01:30:10.688 --> 01:30:15.625
We feared you'd make us all dance.
The von Trapp Family Dancers.

01:30:20.031 --> 01:30:21.726
What are they playing?

01:30:21.966 --> 01:30:24.594
It's the Laendler.
An Austrian folk dance.

01:30:24.802 --> 01:30:27.965
- Show me.
- I haven't danced since I was little.

01:30:28.172 --> 01:30:30.140
You remember. Please?

01:30:30.408 --> 01:30:32.342
- Well...
- Please.

01:30:32.577 --> 01:30:34.807
All right. Come on over here.

01:30:35.313 --> 01:30:38.146
Now you bow and I curtsy.

01:30:39.083 --> 01:30:42.018
- Like this?
- Fine. Now we go for a little walk.

01:30:42.253 --> 01:30:44.915
One, two, three. One, two, three.

01:30:45.223 --> 01:30:49.819
One, two, three, step together.
Now, step hop, step hop.

01:30:50.061 --> 01:30:52.723
Now turn under. Not quite.

01:30:52.930 --> 01:30:56.889
This way. Hop step, hop.
And under.

01:30:57.568 --> 01:30:59.263
Kurt, we'll have to practice.

01:30:59.504 --> 01:31:00.994
Do allow me, will you?

01:32:29.293 --> 01:32:31.158
I don't remember anymore.

01:32:33.331 --> 01:32:35.526
- Your face is all red.
- Is it?

01:32:36.867 --> 01:32:38.960
I don't suppose I'm used to dancing.

01:32:41.672 --> 01:32:43.663
Why, that was beautifully done.

01:32:43.941 --> 01:32:45.841
What a lovely couple you make.

01:32:46.043 --> 01:32:48.170
It's time the children
said good night.

01:32:48.446 --> 01:32:49.777
We'll be in the hall.

01:32:50.014 --> 01:32:52.881
- We have something special prepared.
- Right!

01:32:53.184 --> 01:32:54.344
Yes, come on!

01:33:01.192 --> 01:33:03.524
All that needless worrying, Georg.

01:33:03.794 --> 01:33:06.820
You thought you wouldn't find
a friend at the party.

01:33:09.734 --> 01:33:13.329
- A bit chilly out tonight, isn't it?
- Oh, I don't know.

01:33:13.537 --> 01:33:15.562
It seemed rather warm to me.

01:33:19.744 --> 01:33:20.972
Ladies and gentlemen.

01:33:21.712 --> 01:33:25.808
The children of Captain von Trapp
wish to say good night to you.

01:33:39.930 --> 01:33:43.832
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

01:33:44.035 --> 01:33:47.766
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

01:33:48.039 --> 01:33:52.066
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

01:33:52.276 --> 01:33:54.710
<i>Is popping up to say "coo-coo"</i>

01:33:54.945 --> 01:33:56.606
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:56.881 --> 01:33:58.109
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:58.349 --> 01:34:00.510
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

01:34:00.718 --> 01:34:02.083
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

01:34:02.353 --> 01:34:05.413
<i>To say goodbye</i>

01:34:05.623 --> 01:34:10.925
<i>To you</i>

01:34:14.131 --> 01:34:18.033
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

01:34:18.235 --> 01:34:22.103
<i>I hate to go</i>
<i>And leave this pretty sight</i>

01:34:29.380 --> 01:34:32.713
<i>So long, farewell,</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

01:34:33.384 --> 01:34:36.911
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

01:34:44.261 --> 01:34:48.061
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Au revoir, auf Wiedersehen</i>

01:34:48.332 --> 01:34:52.268
<i>I'd like to stay</i>
<i>And taste my first champagne</i>

01:34:52.503 --> 01:34:54.937
- Yes?
- No.

01:34:59.276 --> 01:35:02.939
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:03.280 --> 01:35:07.239
<i>I leave and heave a sigh</i>
<i>And say goodbye</i>

01:35:07.451 --> 01:35:11.444
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:35:14.492 --> 01:35:17.586
<i>I'm glad to go</i>

01:35:17.828 --> 01:35:20.695
<i>I cannot tell a lie</i>

01:35:21.031 --> 01:35:24.023
<i>I flit, I float</i>

01:35:24.301 --> 01:35:27.759
<i>I fleetly flee, I fly</i>

01:35:37.815 --> 01:35:43.549
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>

01:35:43.788 --> 01:35:47.519
<i>And so must I</i>

01:35:47.725 --> 01:35:50.125
<i>So long</i>

01:35:50.361 --> 01:35:52.921
<i>Farewell</i>

01:35:53.130 --> 01:35:58.534
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:58.803 --> 01:36:04.139
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:04.842 --> 01:36:10.405
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:10.648 --> 01:36:17.520
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:17.721 --> 01:36:26.220
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:31.235 --> 01:36:33.999
Extraordinary!
What they'd do at the festival.

01:36:34.238 --> 01:36:36.729
Young lady,
I must have a word with you.

01:36:37.741 --> 01:36:41.734
Georg, you won't let this girl
get away. She must join the party.

01:36:42.012 --> 01:36:44.412
- No, really l...
- Stop. Stop it now.

01:36:44.682 --> 01:36:47.617
- Georg, please.
- You can if you want to, fräulein.

01:36:47.852 --> 01:36:50.343
I insist.
You will be my dinner partner.

01:36:50.554 --> 01:36:52.454
This is business.
Franz...

01:36:52.723 --> 01:36:55.886
...set another place next to mine
for Fräulein Maria.

01:36:58.062 --> 01:37:00.792
- Whatever you say.
- It appears to be all arranged.

01:37:01.599 --> 01:37:03.464
- It does.
- I'm not suitably dressed.

01:37:04.535 --> 01:37:06.025
You can change. We'll wait.

01:37:09.640 --> 01:37:12.575
Captain, you must be very proud
of your youngsters.

01:37:12.776 --> 01:37:13.640
I am, thank you.

01:37:13.911 --> 01:37:18.473
Is there a more beautiful expression
of what is good in our country...

01:37:18.716 --> 01:37:22.152
...than the innocent voices
of our children?

01:37:22.553 --> 01:37:23.918
Oh, come now, baron.

01:37:24.154 --> 01:37:27.920
Would you have us believe that Austria
holds a monopoly on virtue?

01:37:28.826 --> 01:37:32.956
Herr Zeller, some of us prefer
Austrian voices raised in song...

01:37:33.163 --> 01:37:35.563
...to ugly German threats.

01:37:36.634 --> 01:37:40.263
The ostrich buries his head
in the sand...

01:37:40.471 --> 01:37:43.406
...and sometimes in the flag.

01:37:43.941 --> 01:37:48.139
Perhaps those who would warn you that
the Anschluss is coming, and it is...

01:37:48.412 --> 01:37:52.109
...would get further with you by setting
their words to music.

01:37:52.316 --> 01:37:56.980
If the Nazis take over Austria, you
will be the entire trumpet section.

01:37:57.288 --> 01:37:58.312
You flatter me.

01:37:59.356 --> 01:38:03.258
Oh, how clumsy of me.
I meant to accuse you.

01:38:11.001 --> 01:38:13.492
It's very kind of you
to offer to help me, baroness.

01:38:13.771 --> 01:38:15.329
I'm delighted, Maria.

01:38:15.806 --> 01:38:19.503
I really don't think I have anything
that would be appropriate.

01:38:19.977 --> 01:38:24.107
Now where is that lovely little thing
you were wearing the other evening?

01:38:24.348 --> 01:38:27.647
When the captain couldn't keep
his eyes off you.

01:38:31.021 --> 01:38:32.852
Couldn't keep his eyes off me?

01:38:34.191 --> 01:38:35.988
Come, my dear, we are women.

01:38:36.226 --> 01:38:39.627
Let's not pretend we don't know
when a man notices us.

01:38:39.863 --> 01:38:43.299
- Here we are.
- The captain notices everybody.

01:38:43.867 --> 01:38:46.301
There's no need to feel
so defensive, Maria.

01:38:46.537 --> 01:38:49.005
You are quite attractive, you know.

01:38:49.239 --> 01:38:52.868
The captain would hardly be a man
if he didn't notice you.

01:38:54.478 --> 01:38:56.844
Baroness, I hope you're joking.

01:38:57.314 --> 01:38:58.576
Not at all.

01:38:58.816 --> 01:39:00.408
I've never done a thing to...

01:39:00.684 --> 01:39:02.242
You don't have to, my dear.

01:39:02.886 --> 01:39:07.721
Nothing's more irresistible to a man
than a woman who's in love with him.

01:39:08.993 --> 01:39:11.427
- In love with him?
- Of course.

01:39:12.363 --> 01:39:15.764
What makes it so nice is
he thinks he's in love with you.

01:39:18.502 --> 01:39:20.094
But that's not true.

01:39:20.504 --> 01:39:23.996
Surely you've noticed the way
he looks into your eyes.

01:39:24.274 --> 01:39:29.177
And you know, you blushed in his arms
when you were dancing just now.

01:39:30.414 --> 01:39:32.109
Don't take it to heart.

01:39:32.383 --> 01:39:34.681
He'll get over it soon enough,
I think.

01:39:34.952 --> 01:39:36.920
Men do, you know.

01:39:37.921 --> 01:39:39.013
Then I should go.

01:39:40.357 --> 01:39:41.790
I mustn't stay here.

01:39:52.269 --> 01:39:55.705
- Is there something I can do to help?
- No, nothing.

01:39:57.474 --> 01:39:58.702
Yes.

01:39:59.710 --> 01:40:01.735
Don't say a word to the captain.

01:40:03.380 --> 01:40:06.941
No, I wouldn't dream of it.

01:40:13.724 --> 01:40:15.282
Goodbye, Maria.

01:40:16.093 --> 01:40:18.891
I'm sure you'll make a very fine nun.

01:40:48.926 --> 01:40:50.917
Champagne, darling.

01:40:51.328 --> 01:40:55.321
I feel like celebrating. Cheers.

01:41:00.804 --> 01:41:03.705
- You know something.
- Perhaps.

01:41:03.941 --> 01:41:08.469
If you're so clever, tell me how to
get fräulein to influence Georg.

01:41:08.712 --> 01:41:11.340
I want those children in the festival.

01:41:11.815 --> 01:41:14.113
Elsa, this is important to Austria.

01:41:14.318 --> 01:41:16.013
Wouldn't do you any harm either.

01:41:16.220 --> 01:41:17.812
I thought of that.

01:41:18.055 --> 01:41:20.523
Well, if it's a matter of influence...

01:41:20.724 --> 01:41:23.625
...maybe the one you have
to be talking to is me.

01:44:48.558 --> 01:44:50.788
- Two.
- Three.

01:44:51.060 --> 01:44:52.550
- Four.
- Five.

01:44:53.796 --> 01:44:55.821
- Six.
- Seven.

01:44:56.098 --> 01:44:57.725
Eight.

01:44:57.967 --> 01:44:59.798
- Four.
- Two.

01:45:00.903 --> 01:45:02.734
- Seven.
- Five.

01:45:02.972 --> 01:45:05.167
- Two.
- Six.

01:45:09.812 --> 01:45:11.837
Isn't this fun?

01:45:13.249 --> 01:45:15.581
- Four.
- I'm number five.

01:45:15.851 --> 01:45:18.012
- Oh, yes.
- Eight.

01:45:18.321 --> 01:45:20.687
- Two.
- Four.

01:45:21.090 --> 01:45:22.318
Six.

01:45:24.794 --> 01:45:26.022
Two.

01:45:27.163 --> 01:45:30.132
Baroness Schraeder, do you mind
if we stop now? We're tired.

01:45:30.366 --> 01:45:32.334
Whatever you want, dear.

01:45:32.602 --> 01:45:34.593
We'll do it again tomorrow.

01:45:44.780 --> 01:45:46.941
The country's so restful, isn't it?

01:45:47.984 --> 01:45:49.611
Have some lemonade.

01:45:50.853 --> 01:45:52.286
There must be an easier way.

01:45:53.689 --> 01:45:56.954
I get a fiendish delight thinking
of you as the mother of seven.

01:45:57.893 --> 01:45:59.724
How do you plan to do it?

01:45:59.996 --> 01:46:02.021
Darling, haven't you ever heard...

01:46:02.298 --> 01:46:05.392
...of a delightful little thing
called boarding school?

01:46:06.535 --> 01:46:08.799
Baroness Machiavelli.

01:46:10.139 --> 01:46:12.130
Uncle Max, where's Father?

01:46:12.408 --> 01:46:14.205
I think he's in the house.

01:46:14.410 --> 01:46:16.970
What's the matter
with all you gloomy pussies?

01:46:17.213 --> 01:46:20.011
- Nothing.
- I know. Let's have a rehearsal.

01:46:20.216 --> 01:46:21.114
What for?

01:46:21.317 --> 01:46:23.808
Let's make believe we're on-stage
at the festival.

01:46:24.020 --> 01:46:27.888
- I don't feel like singing.
- Not without Fräulein Maria.

01:46:28.157 --> 01:46:30.557
Liesl, get the guitar.
Come on, Marta.

01:46:30.760 --> 01:46:33.729
Everybody into the group.
Get in your places.

01:46:33.996 --> 01:46:36.760
Now be cheerful, right?
Give us the key, Liesl.

01:46:38.668 --> 01:46:41.330
Now, impress me.

01:46:45.341 --> 01:46:46.672
Gretl, why don't you sing?

01:46:46.942 --> 01:46:49.410
I can't. I've got a sore finger.

01:46:50.446 --> 01:46:53.506
But you sang so beautifully
the night of the party.

01:46:53.716 --> 01:46:56.048
Come on, all of you.
Try something you know.

01:46:56.285 --> 01:46:57.775
Enjoy it. Be cheerful.

01:46:58.054 --> 01:46:59.681
All right, Liesl.

01:47:01.624 --> 01:47:07.028
<i>The hills are alive</i>

01:47:07.263 --> 01:47:14.931
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:16.138 --> 01:47:21.201
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

01:47:21.444 --> 01:47:29.283
<i>For a thousand years</i>

01:47:29.985 --> 01:47:35.389
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

01:47:35.624 --> 01:47:43.326
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:43.666 --> 01:47:46.294
They wanted to sing for me,
bless their hearts.

01:47:46.602 --> 01:47:48.502
That's lovely, lovely.
Don't stop.

01:47:52.508 --> 01:47:56.410
- Something long and cool, Georg?
- No, thank you, darling.

01:47:56.812 --> 01:47:59.246
- Father?
- Yes, Brigitta?

01:47:59.682 --> 01:48:01.946
Is it true Fräulein Maria
isn't coming back?

01:48:02.251 --> 01:48:05.345
Yes, I suppose it's true.
What have we got here?

01:48:05.654 --> 01:48:10.353
- Pink lemonade.
- Laced with lemonade.

01:48:11.093 --> 01:48:12.617
I don't believe it, Father.

01:48:13.996 --> 01:48:16.021
- What?
- About Fräulein Maria.

01:48:16.432 --> 01:48:17.660
Oh, Fräulein Maria!

01:48:17.967 --> 01:48:21.425
Didn't I tell you what her note said?
I'm sure I did.

01:48:22.171 --> 01:48:24.662
She said she missed her life
at the abbey.

01:48:24.940 --> 01:48:27.101
She had to leave us.

01:48:27.343 --> 01:48:28.935
And that's all there is to it.

01:48:30.646 --> 01:48:33.342
I think I'm brave enough to try
some of that.

01:48:33.549 --> 01:48:36.279
- She didn't even say goodbye.
- She did in her note.

01:48:36.552 --> 01:48:38.349
That isn't the same thing.

01:48:38.654 --> 01:48:40.281
Not too sweet, not too sour.

01:48:41.023 --> 01:48:43.014
Just too pink.

01:48:44.460 --> 01:48:47.554
Father, who is our new governess
going to be?

01:48:54.203 --> 01:48:55.295
Well...

01:48:57.640 --> 01:49:02.873
...you're not going to have
a governess anymore.

01:49:03.212 --> 01:49:05.874
- We're not?
- No.

01:49:08.083 --> 01:49:10.210
You're going to have a new mother.

01:49:11.320 --> 01:49:13.345
A new mother?

01:49:14.190 --> 01:49:17.318
We talked about it last night.
It's all settled.

01:49:17.526 --> 01:49:20.222
And we're all going to be very happy.

01:49:53.229 --> 01:49:55.697
Well, all right, all right.
Run off and play.

01:50:27.663 --> 01:50:28.630
Yes, my children?

01:50:28.831 --> 01:50:31.231
- My name is Liesl.
- Yes, Liesl?

01:50:31.734 --> 01:50:35.670
We, my brothers and sisters,
want to see Fräulein Maria.

01:50:36.839 --> 01:50:38.830
Fräulein Maria?

01:50:39.608 --> 01:50:41.576
Oh, Maria.

01:50:43.479 --> 01:50:45.310
Come in, please.

01:50:49.184 --> 01:50:50.742
Wait here.

01:51:01.697 --> 01:51:04.860
I'm Sister Margaretta. I understand
you inquired about Maria.

01:51:05.134 --> 01:51:07.625
We have to see her.
Will you tell her we're here?

01:51:07.870 --> 01:51:10.464
- I'm afraid I can't do that.
- But you've got to!

01:51:10.773 --> 01:51:12.832
- She's our governess.
- We want her back.

01:51:13.042 --> 01:51:14.942
She didn't even say goodbye.

01:51:15.177 --> 01:51:16.940
All we want to do is talk to her.

01:51:17.713 --> 01:51:20.614
I'm very sorry,
but Maria is in seclusion.

01:51:20.849 --> 01:51:23.943
- She hasn't been seeing anyone.
- She'll see us.

01:51:24.186 --> 01:51:26.677
I want to show her my finger.

01:51:26.889 --> 01:51:28.789
Some other time, dear.

01:51:29.058 --> 01:51:30.355
I'll tell her you were here.

01:51:30.626 --> 01:51:33.686
- It was sweet of you to call.
- We have to speak to her!

01:51:34.330 --> 01:51:37.458
Run along, children.
Run along home.

01:51:37.666 --> 01:51:39.293
I'm sure she'd like to see us.

01:51:39.568 --> 01:51:41.832
Sister Margaretta, please.

01:51:42.071 --> 01:51:45.802
- Goodbye, children.
- Sister Margaretta, may we, please?

01:51:48.577 --> 01:51:50.306
What was that about, Sister?

01:51:50.546 --> 01:51:52.741
The von Trapp children,
Reverend Mother.

01:51:52.982 --> 01:51:55.416
They want to see Maria.

01:51:55.684 --> 01:51:57.982
Has she spoken yet?
Has she told you anything?

01:51:58.253 --> 01:52:02.246
She doesn't say a word,
Reverend Mother, except in prayer.

01:52:02.524 --> 01:52:03.513
Poor child.

01:52:03.726 --> 01:52:06.695
It's strange.
She seems happy to be back here...

01:52:06.929 --> 01:52:10.228
...and yet she's unhappy too.

01:52:11.500 --> 01:52:14.560
Perhaps I have been wrong
in leaving her alone so long.

01:52:14.837 --> 01:52:17.533
Bring her to me,
even if she's not yet ready.

01:52:17.740 --> 01:52:19.401
Yes, Reverend Mother.

01:52:24.913 --> 01:52:28.405
Sister Augusta, take our new postulant
to the robing room.

01:52:29.418 --> 01:52:31.682
God bless you, my daughter.

01:52:37.893 --> 01:52:39.622
Yes, bring her in.

01:52:48.637 --> 01:52:50.901
You've been unhappy. I'm sorry.

01:52:52.941 --> 01:52:54.135
Reverend Mother.

01:52:54.476 --> 01:52:57.104
Why did they send you back to us?

01:52:57.946 --> 01:52:59.914
They didn't send me back.
I left.

01:53:02.418 --> 01:53:03.976
Sit down, Maria.

01:53:04.486 --> 01:53:06.283
Tell me what happened.

01:53:11.493 --> 01:53:12.824
I was frightened.

01:53:13.095 --> 01:53:17.555
- Frightened? Were they unkind to you.
- Oh, no!

01:53:17.800 --> 01:53:21.497
No, I was confused. I felt...

01:53:22.971 --> 01:53:25.064
I've never felt that way before.

01:53:25.307 --> 01:53:29.073
I couldn't stay. I knew that here
I'd be away from it. I'd be safe.

01:53:29.311 --> 01:53:34.010
Maria, our abbey is not to be used
as an escape.

01:53:34.283 --> 01:53:36.513
What is it you can't face?

01:53:38.487 --> 01:53:39.920
I can't face him again.

01:53:40.756 --> 01:53:42.280
Him?

01:53:43.859 --> 01:53:45.918
Thank you, Sister Margaretta.

01:53:55.537 --> 01:53:57.164
Captain von Trapp?

01:54:02.611 --> 01:54:05.307
- Are you in love with him?
- I don't know!

01:54:05.547 --> 01:54:07.014
I don't know. I...

01:54:07.549 --> 01:54:11.383
The baroness said I was.
She said that he was in love with me.

01:54:11.653 --> 01:54:14.315
But I didn't want to believe it.

01:54:15.390 --> 01:54:17.688
There were times we looked
at each other.

01:54:17.893 --> 01:54:19.451
I could hardly breathe.

01:54:19.828 --> 01:54:22.524
- Did you let him see your feelings?
- I don't know.

01:54:23.132 --> 01:54:25.794
That's what's torturing me.
I was on God's errand.

01:54:26.001 --> 01:54:30.995
To have asked for his love would have
been wrong. I just couldn't stay.

01:54:33.175 --> 01:54:35.973
I'm ready at this moment
to take my vows.

01:54:36.845 --> 01:54:39.905
- Please help me.
- Maria.

01:54:41.483 --> 01:54:46.182
The love of a man and a woman is holy.
You have a great capacity to love.

01:54:46.421 --> 01:54:49.356
You must find out how God
wants you to spend your love.

01:54:49.658 --> 01:54:53.492
But I pledged my life to God.
I pledged my life to his service.

01:54:53.695 --> 01:54:58.064
My daughter, if you love this man,
it doesn't mean you love God less.

01:54:59.735 --> 01:55:01.600
No.

01:55:01.837 --> 01:55:03.702
You must find out.

01:55:05.440 --> 01:55:07.931
You must go back.

01:55:08.210 --> 01:55:10.178
You can't ask me to do that.

01:55:10.379 --> 01:55:12.870
- Please let me stay. I beg...
- Maria.

01:55:13.081 --> 01:55:17.040
These walls were not built
to shut out problems.

01:55:17.252 --> 01:55:18.844
You have to face them.

01:55:19.421 --> 01:55:22.686
You have to live the life
you were born to live.

01:55:28.564 --> 01:55:32.864
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:33.101 --> 01:55:36.867
<i>Search high and low</i>

01:55:37.105 --> 01:55:41.872
<i>Follow every byway</i>

01:55:42.110 --> 01:55:46.376
<i>Every path you know</i>

01:55:46.815 --> 01:55:51.275
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:51.553 --> 01:55:55.887
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:55:56.124 --> 01:56:00.493
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:00.762 --> 01:56:05.096
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:05.300 --> 01:56:08.394
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:08.637 --> 01:56:13.472
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:14.243 --> 01:56:17.644
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:56:17.913 --> 01:56:24.318
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:56:24.620 --> 01:56:28.920
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:56:29.157 --> 01:56:33.491
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:56:33.762 --> 01:56:38.324
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:38.533 --> 01:56:46.941
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:48.043 --> 01:56:51.535
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:51.847 --> 01:56:57.376
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:57.653 --> 01:57:01.145
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:57:01.390 --> 01:57:07.818
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:57:08.063 --> 01:57:12.500
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:57:12.734 --> 01:57:16.670
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:57:17.339 --> 01:57:21.969
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:57:22.377 --> 01:57:26.473
<i>Till you find...</i>

01:57:26.715 --> 01:57:36.716
<i>...your dream</i>

01:57:39.261 --> 01:57:42.822
Now, it's not like my children
to be secretive.

01:57:43.065 --> 01:57:45.158
We're not being secretive, Father.

01:57:46.835 --> 01:57:50.168
And it's not like my children
to be late for dinner.

01:57:50.439 --> 01:57:53.875
- We lost track of the time.
- I see.

01:57:54.676 --> 01:57:58.077
Who's going to be the first one
to tell me the truth? Friedrich.

01:57:58.347 --> 01:58:00.406
Brigitta. Liesl.

01:58:01.783 --> 01:58:04.013
Where do you think we were, Father?

01:58:10.592 --> 01:58:14.551
If you don't believe us, you must have
some idea of where you think we were.

01:58:18.133 --> 01:58:19.930
- Marta.
- Yes, Father.

01:58:20.135 --> 01:58:21.397
You tell me.

01:58:22.738 --> 01:58:26.367
Friedrich told you, Father.
We were berry picking.

01:58:27.209 --> 01:58:31.873
- I forgot! You were berry picking.
- Yes, we love berry picking.

01:58:32.114 --> 01:58:33.206
All afternoon?

01:58:33.448 --> 01:58:35.177
- We picked thousands.
- Thousands?

01:58:35.384 --> 01:58:38.285
- They were all over the place.
- What kind of berries?

01:58:38.553 --> 01:58:41.818
- Blueberries, sir.
- Blueberries.

01:58:43.759 --> 01:58:47.126
It's too early for blueberries.

01:58:48.630 --> 01:58:50.723
- They were strawberries.
- Strawberries?

01:58:51.433 --> 01:58:54.129
It's been so cold lately,
they turned blue.

01:58:59.975 --> 01:59:02.136
Very well. Show me the berries.

01:59:03.412 --> 01:59:04.606
- We...
- Well...

01:59:04.846 --> 01:59:07.610
- Show me the berries you picked.
- We don't have them.

01:59:07.849 --> 01:59:10.113
You don't have them?
What happened to them?

01:59:10.352 --> 01:59:13.150
- We...
- We ate them.

01:59:13.355 --> 01:59:15.949
- You ate them?
- Yes!

01:59:16.158 --> 01:59:17.750
- They were so good.
- Delicious.

01:59:17.993 --> 01:59:19.187
Very well.

01:59:19.461 --> 01:59:24.592
Since you've obviously stuffed
yourselves on thousands of berries...

01:59:24.833 --> 01:59:28.769
...you can't be hungry anymore,
so I'll have to tell Frau Schmidt...

01:59:29.004 --> 01:59:31.871
...to skip your dinner.

01:59:41.049 --> 01:59:43.847
It's your fault.
We should have told him the truth.

01:59:44.119 --> 01:59:46.087
And made him boiling mad at us?

01:59:46.288 --> 01:59:48.222
It's better than starving to death.

01:59:48.457 --> 01:59:51.324
We didn't do anything wrong.
We just wanted to see her.

01:59:52.627 --> 01:59:55.721
My stomach's making noises.

01:59:56.164 --> 01:59:58.997
The least they could have done
was to let us say hello.

02:00:00.135 --> 02:00:04.037
- I wonder what grass tastes like.
- I feel awful.

02:00:04.473 --> 02:00:08.739
When Fräulein Maria wanted to feel
better she used to sing that song.

02:00:09.344 --> 02:00:10.811
Let's try it.

02:00:11.046 --> 02:00:13.708
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>

02:00:14.015 --> 02:00:18.042
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

02:00:18.887 --> 02:00:21.481
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>

02:00:21.690 --> 02:00:24.750
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

02:00:26.094 --> 02:00:32.055
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

02:00:32.334 --> 02:00:38.330
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:00:38.573 --> 02:00:40.598
Why don't I feel better?

02:00:41.776 --> 02:00:44.074
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>

02:00:44.346 --> 02:00:47.440
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

02:00:47.716 --> 02:00:53.348
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

02:00:53.722 --> 02:00:56.885
- <i>Silver white winters...</i>
- Fräulein Maria's back!

02:00:57.092 --> 02:00:58.389
<i>...that melt into springs</i>

02:00:58.793 --> 02:01:02.058
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:01:02.297 --> 02:01:05.391
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

02:01:05.600 --> 02:01:07.727
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

02:01:08.236 --> 02:01:11.205
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

02:01:11.473 --> 02:01:13.737
<i>And then I don't feel</i>

02:01:13.942 --> 02:01:20.711
<i>So bad</i>

02:01:20.949 --> 02:01:23.975
- Children, I'm so glad to see you.
- We missed you.

02:01:24.219 --> 02:01:25.208
I missed you.

02:01:25.487 --> 02:01:27.614
- Kurt, how are you?
- Hungry.

02:01:29.157 --> 02:01:31.785
- What happened to your finger?
- It got caught.

02:01:32.060 --> 02:01:34.221
- Caught in what?
- Friedrich's teeth.

02:01:35.463 --> 02:01:37.624
- Liesl, you all right?
- Just fair.

02:01:37.832 --> 02:01:40.824
- Any telegrams been delivered lately?
- None at all.

02:01:41.069 --> 02:01:44.505
But I'm learning to accept it.
I'll be glad when school begins.

02:01:44.806 --> 02:01:49.505
Liesl, you can't use school to escape
your problems. You have to face them.

02:01:49.744 --> 02:01:51.177
I have so much to tell you.

02:01:51.446 --> 02:01:53.437
We have things to tell you too.

02:01:53.782 --> 02:01:57.479
The most important thing is
that Father is going to be married.

02:01:57.686 --> 02:01:58.744
Married?

02:01:59.087 --> 02:02:01.112
Yes, to Baroness Schraeder.

02:02:09.030 --> 02:02:10.588
Oh, I see.

02:02:12.434 --> 02:02:15.801
Father, look!
Fräulein Maria's back!

02:02:16.037 --> 02:02:18.096
Fräulein Maria's back from the abbey.

02:02:20.308 --> 02:02:21.366
Good evening, captain.

02:02:22.844 --> 02:02:24.141
Good evening.

02:02:26.681 --> 02:02:28.512
Everyone inside for dinner.

02:02:28.817 --> 02:02:30.375
Dinner!

02:02:39.728 --> 02:02:44.461
You left without saying goodbye.
Even to the children.

02:02:45.467 --> 02:02:46.991
It was wrong of me. Forgive me.

02:02:49.037 --> 02:02:50.197
Why did you?

02:02:50.405 --> 02:02:53.238
Please don't ask me.
The reason no longer exists.

02:02:54.409 --> 02:02:57.503
Fräulein Maria, you've returned.

02:02:58.747 --> 02:03:00.544
Isn't it wonderful, Georg?

02:03:03.852 --> 02:03:06.082
I wish you every happiness,
baroness.

02:03:06.321 --> 02:03:09.017
You too, captain.
The children say you're to marry.

02:03:09.257 --> 02:03:10.383
Thank you, my dear.

02:03:12.927 --> 02:03:16.488
You are back to stay?

02:03:18.566 --> 02:03:21.899
Only until arrangements can be made
for another governess.

02:04:17.592 --> 02:04:19.219
There you are.

02:04:33.608 --> 02:04:36.076
I must speak to cook
about the schnitzel.

02:04:36.344 --> 02:04:39.643
It is entirely too delicious
for my figure.

02:04:40.081 --> 02:04:43.016
And it makes you much too quiet
at the dinner table.

02:04:43.284 --> 02:04:45.275
Or was it the wine?

02:04:45.520 --> 02:04:47.351
Undoubtedly the wine.

02:04:49.924 --> 02:04:52.188
You have no idea
the trouble I'm having...

02:04:52.460 --> 02:04:55.190
...trying to decide on
a wedding present for you.

02:04:55.497 --> 02:04:57.658
Oh, I know. I'm enough.

02:04:57.932 --> 02:05:01.527
But I do want you to have
some little trifle for the occasion.

02:05:01.770 --> 02:05:04.102
At first I thought
of a fountain pen...

02:05:04.339 --> 02:05:06.603
...but you've already got one.

02:05:06.875 --> 02:05:09.810
Then I thought perhaps a villa
in the south of France...

02:05:10.044 --> 02:05:12.706
...but they are so difficult
to gift-wrap.

02:05:12.981 --> 02:05:15.381
Oh, Georg, how do you
feel about yachts?

02:05:15.683 --> 02:05:17.947
A long, sleek one
for the Mediterranean...

02:05:18.186 --> 02:05:20.950
...or a tiny one
for your bathtub, huh?

02:05:23.124 --> 02:05:25.149
- Elsa.
- Where to go on our honeymoon?

02:05:25.393 --> 02:05:26.985
Now, that's a real problem.

02:05:27.195 --> 02:05:30.562
A trip around the world
would be lovely. And then I said:

02:05:30.865 --> 02:05:33.698
"Oh, Elsa, there must be
someplace better to go."

02:05:33.968 --> 02:05:36.402
- But don't worry, darling, I'll...
- Elsa.

02:05:37.071 --> 02:05:38.333
Yes, Georg.

02:05:39.340 --> 02:05:40.671
It's no use...

02:05:41.876 --> 02:05:43.241
...you and I.

02:05:44.813 --> 02:05:48.044
I'm being dishonest to both of us...

02:05:49.384 --> 02:05:51.045
...and utterly unfair to you.

02:05:56.324 --> 02:05:59.054
- When two people talk of marriage...
- No, don't.

02:05:59.928 --> 02:06:02.021
Don't say another word, please.

02:06:05.333 --> 02:06:10.361
You see, there are other things
I've been thinking of.

02:06:11.272 --> 02:06:16.005
Fond as I am of you, I really don't
think you're the right man for me.

02:06:18.546 --> 02:06:21.037
You're much too independent.

02:06:21.349 --> 02:06:26.048
And I need someone
who needs me desperately...

02:06:26.354 --> 02:06:29.346
...or at least needs
my money desperately.

02:06:31.526 --> 02:06:36.429
I've enjoyed every moment we've had
together and I do thank you for that.

02:06:39.200 --> 02:06:41.100
Now, if you'll forgive me...

02:06:41.302 --> 02:06:43.361
...I'll go inside,
pack my little bags...

02:06:43.605 --> 02:06:46.096
...and return to Vienna
where I belong.

02:06:51.479 --> 02:06:53.310
And somewhere out there...

02:06:53.615 --> 02:06:57.984
...is a young lady who, I think...

02:06:58.253 --> 02:06:59.481
...will never be a nun.

02:07:11.633 --> 02:07:13.965
Auf Wiedersehen, darling.

02:07:39.694 --> 02:07:40.854
Hello.

02:07:46.668 --> 02:07:50.263
I thought I just might find you here.

02:07:54.442 --> 02:07:56.706
Was there something you wanted?

02:07:57.145 --> 02:08:00.273
No, no, no. Sit down, please.

02:08:01.215 --> 02:08:02.546
Please.

02:08:07.689 --> 02:08:09.020
May I?

02:08:21.402 --> 02:08:26.135
You know, I was thinking
and I was wondering two things:

02:08:27.308 --> 02:08:31.540
Why did you run away to the abbey?

02:08:32.380 --> 02:08:37.044
And what was it
that made you come back?

02:08:38.720 --> 02:08:43.180
Well, I had an obligation
to fulfill...

02:08:43.391 --> 02:08:45.518
...and I came back to fulfill it.

02:08:46.160 --> 02:08:47.593
Is that all?

02:08:48.930 --> 02:08:51.091
And I missed the children.

02:08:51.432 --> 02:08:52.592
Yes.

02:08:53.868 --> 02:08:56.769
- Only the children?
- No. Yes.

02:08:57.005 --> 02:09:00.839
- Isn't it right that I missed them?
- Oh, yes. Yes, of course.

02:09:01.042 --> 02:09:03.670
I was only hoping that perhaps you...

02:09:04.779 --> 02:09:06.542
Perhaps you might...

02:09:08.282 --> 02:09:09.510
Yes?

02:09:11.285 --> 02:09:16.587
Well, nothing was the same
when you were away...

02:09:17.358 --> 02:09:20.589
...and it'll be all wrong again
after you leave...

02:09:20.795 --> 02:09:25.459
...and I just thought perhaps
you might change your mind.

02:09:29.537 --> 02:09:33.769
Well, I'm sure the baroness will be
able to make things fine for you.

02:09:34.042 --> 02:09:35.373
Maria...

02:09:37.478 --> 02:09:40.970
- There isn't going to be any baroness.
- There isn't?

02:09:43.384 --> 02:09:44.749
No.

02:09:45.053 --> 02:09:46.816
I don't understand.

02:09:49.223 --> 02:09:53.319
Well, we've called off our engagement,
you see, and...

02:09:53.594 --> 02:09:57.052
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Yes. You are?

02:09:58.232 --> 02:10:00.325
- You did?
- Yes.

02:10:01.469 --> 02:10:05.997
Well, you can't marry someone
when you're...

02:10:08.576 --> 02:10:10.635
...in love with someone else...

02:10:14.015 --> 02:10:15.448
...can you?

02:10:50.318 --> 02:10:52.616
The Reverend Mother always says:

02:10:52.854 --> 02:10:56.290
"When the Lord closes a door,
somewhere He opens a window."

02:11:04.699 --> 02:11:07.725
What else does
the Reverend Mother say?

02:11:08.669 --> 02:11:11.069
That you have to look for your life.

02:11:12.740 --> 02:11:15.300
Is that why you came back?

02:11:19.347 --> 02:11:20.814
And have you found it...

02:11:21.816 --> 02:11:22.976
...Maria?

02:11:24.752 --> 02:11:26.743
I think I have.

02:11:29.490 --> 02:11:30.889
I know I have.

02:11:33.394 --> 02:11:35.055
I love you.

02:11:39.033 --> 02:11:40.898
Oh, can this be happening to me?

02:11:44.272 --> 02:11:49.676
<i>Perhaps I had a wicked childhood</i>

02:11:51.179 --> 02:11:56.412
<i>Perhaps I had a miserable youth</i>

02:11:58.286 --> 02:12:04.225
<i>But somewhere</i>
<i>In my wicked, miserable past</i>

02:12:04.725 --> 02:12:10.527
<i>There must have been a moment of truth</i>

02:12:11.465 --> 02:12:18.234
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:12:18.973 --> 02:12:24.969
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:12:25.613 --> 02:12:32.416
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:12:33.287 --> 02:12:40.921
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:12:42.163 --> 02:12:45.132
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:12:46.267 --> 02:12:50.135
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:12:50.972 --> 02:12:59.846
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:01.415 --> 02:13:10.915
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:13:11.792 --> 02:13:16.627
Do you know when I first
started loving you?

02:13:17.031 --> 02:13:20.933
That night at dinner, when you sat
on that ridiculous pine cone.

02:13:21.168 --> 02:13:22.465
What?

02:13:23.804 --> 02:13:27.262
I knew the first time you blew
that silly whistle.

02:13:28.175 --> 02:13:30.166
Oh, my love.

02:13:33.948 --> 02:13:41.855
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:13:43.824 --> 02:13:49.660
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:13:51.032 --> 02:13:58.063
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:58.873 --> 02:14:06.575
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:14:07.748 --> 02:14:11.240
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:14:11.986 --> 02:14:15.012
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:14:15.256 --> 02:14:21.058
<i>So somewhere in my youth...</i>

02:14:21.329 --> 02:14:23.559
<i>...or childhood</i>

02:14:26.667 --> 02:14:33.197
<i>I must have done something</i>

02:14:35.242 --> 02:14:47.882
<i>Something good</i>

02:14:54.595 --> 02:14:56.119
Maria.

02:14:57.965 --> 02:15:02.561
Is there anyone I should go to,
to ask permission to marry you?

02:15:06.474 --> 02:15:09.034
- Why don't we ask...
- The children?

02:16:57.551 --> 02:17:01.578
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:02.389 --> 02:17:06.086
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

02:17:07.061 --> 02:17:11.225
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

02:17:11.665 --> 02:17:12.654
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

02:17:12.900 --> 02:17:16.165
<i>A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>A clown</i>

02:17:16.370 --> 02:17:20.932
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

02:17:21.375 --> 02:17:25.402
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

02:17:26.113 --> 02:17:30.413
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

02:17:30.784 --> 02:17:34.720
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

02:17:35.055 --> 02:17:40.049
<i>Oh, how do you solve</i>
<i>A problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:40.427 --> 02:17:47.060
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam</i>
<i>In your hand?</i>

02:19:53.160 --> 02:19:54.718
Herr Detweiler!

02:19:57.331 --> 02:19:59.993
- Heil Hitler.
- Oh, good afternoon, Herr Zeller.

02:20:00.234 --> 02:20:03.533
Perhaps you've not heard.
I am now the Gauleiter.

02:20:03.837 --> 02:20:05.361
Heil Hitler.

02:20:06.273 --> 02:20:07.433
Heil Hitler.

02:20:07.741 --> 02:20:10.005
I've come from
Captain von Trapp's house.

02:20:10.444 --> 02:20:14.039
The only one in the area
not flying the Third Reich flag...

02:20:14.281 --> 02:20:15.543
...since the Anschluss.

02:20:15.749 --> 02:20:17.910
- But we have dealt with that.
- I don't...

02:20:18.185 --> 02:20:21.120
The housekeeper told me
that I would find you here.

02:20:21.388 --> 02:20:23.083
The only thing she'd tell me.

02:20:23.590 --> 02:20:26.115
What kind of information
are you looking for?

02:20:26.393 --> 02:20:28.258
When will the captain return?

02:20:28.796 --> 02:20:32.732
Well, he's on his honeymoon trip.
He's not been in touch with us.

02:20:32.966 --> 02:20:37.801
Am I to believe he hasn't communicated
with his children in over a month?

02:20:38.072 --> 02:20:39.972
How many men do you know...

02:20:40.240 --> 02:20:43.539
...who communicate with their children
while honeymooning?

02:20:44.445 --> 02:20:48.142
Upon his return, he'll fill
his proper position in the new order.

02:20:48.449 --> 02:20:50.815
Naturally.
And may I congratulate you...

02:20:51.051 --> 02:20:55.715
...and your people in allowing the
festival to go on tonight as planned.

02:20:56.256 --> 02:20:59.714
Why should it not go on?
Nothing in Austria has changed.

02:20:59.960 --> 02:21:03.361
Singing and music will
show this to the world.

02:21:03.564 --> 02:21:05.259
Austria is the same.

02:21:06.133 --> 02:21:07.498
Heil Hitler.

02:21:09.670 --> 02:21:11.262
Heil Hitler.

02:21:12.940 --> 02:21:14.168
Come, let's go home.

02:21:14.408 --> 02:21:17.900
- Why was he so cross?
- Everybody's cross these days.

02:21:18.112 --> 02:21:21.479
Maybe the flag with the black spider
makes people nervous.

02:21:21.682 --> 02:21:24.617
- Will Father be in trouble?
- He doesn't have to be.

02:21:24.852 --> 02:21:27.582
The thing to do
is to get along with everybody.

02:21:27.821 --> 02:21:30.016
Remember that tonight at the concert.

02:21:30.257 --> 02:21:33.158
Are we really going to sing
before a lot of people?

02:21:33.360 --> 02:21:35.453
Look. The von Trapp Family Singers:

02:21:35.662 --> 02:21:40.258
Liesl, Friedrich, Louisa, Brigitta,
Kurt, Marta and Gretl.

02:21:40.467 --> 02:21:44.836
- Why am I always last?
- Because you are the most important.

02:21:45.539 --> 02:21:47.166
There we go.

02:21:53.046 --> 02:21:56.504
Are you sure Father will approve
of our singing in public?

02:21:56.717 --> 02:21:59.015
He'll be pleased and proud.

02:21:59.486 --> 02:22:01.954
- Liesl, do you think so?
- Don't you trust me?

02:22:02.156 --> 02:22:03.180
No.

02:22:03.390 --> 02:22:05.483
You're a very intelligent girl.

02:22:06.026 --> 02:22:08.187
Liesl. Liesl!

02:22:09.129 --> 02:22:10.323
Rolfe!

02:22:11.331 --> 02:22:13.356
I'm so glad to see you.
It's been su...

02:22:13.567 --> 02:22:14.659
Good afternoon.

02:22:15.068 --> 02:22:18.003
Give this to your father
as soon as he's home.

02:22:18.672 --> 02:22:20.537
- He's on his honeymoon.
- I know.

02:22:20.741 --> 02:22:24.074
- You do?
- We make it our business to know all.

02:22:24.812 --> 02:22:27.372
- Who's "we"?
- See that he gets it.

02:22:27.581 --> 02:22:29.913
- What is it?
- It's a telegram from Berlin.

02:22:30.751 --> 02:22:33.242
Don't you want to deliver it yourself?

02:22:33.720 --> 02:22:36.348
I'm occupied
with more important matters.

02:22:36.557 --> 02:22:39.048
And your father had better be too.

02:22:39.326 --> 02:22:40.816
But, Rolfe!

02:23:03.917 --> 02:23:05.578
Father!

02:23:05.853 --> 02:23:08.515
- We didn't expect you so soon.
- Hello, hello!

02:23:08.755 --> 02:23:11.553
We didn't expect you home
until next week!

02:23:11.758 --> 02:23:17.196
- Did you bring souvenirs from Paris?
- Hello! How are you?

02:23:18.298 --> 02:23:19.595
Why didn't you call us?

02:23:19.800 --> 02:23:21.734
We couldn't get through.

02:23:22.035 --> 02:23:23.969
I had nothing to do with that.

02:23:24.238 --> 02:23:26.263
We came back as fast as we could.

02:23:26.573 --> 02:23:28.734
Well, well, well! We missed you!

02:23:28.976 --> 02:23:31.410
- We missed you!
- We missed kissing you.

02:23:31.612 --> 02:23:34.445
We missed all the noise
in the morning.

02:23:34.715 --> 02:23:38.913
- Mostly, we missed hearing you sing.
- Oh, you came back just in time.

02:23:39.119 --> 02:23:40.882
Look, Fräulein Maria...

02:23:41.088 --> 02:23:42.715
I mean Mother.

02:23:43.123 --> 02:23:45.614
We're going to sing
in the festival tonight.

02:23:45.826 --> 02:23:47.953
We've been having a lovely time!

02:23:48.228 --> 02:23:50.287
We've been rehearsing all...

02:23:51.798 --> 02:23:54.130
Surprise! Surprise!

02:23:54.801 --> 02:23:57.292
Surprises for you on the terrace.

02:24:00.340 --> 02:24:01.739
We'll talk about this.

02:24:01.942 --> 02:24:06.242
I would've told you but you were away.
I had to make a last-minute decision.

02:24:06.513 --> 02:24:09.004
I was fortunate to enter them at all.

02:24:09.249 --> 02:24:13.982
They'll be the talk of the festival.
Imagine, seven children in one family!

02:24:14.187 --> 02:24:15.814
Max!

02:24:16.423 --> 02:24:19.256
Somehow I recall having made it
quite clear to you...

02:24:19.526 --> 02:24:22.188
...how I feel about my family
singing in public!

02:24:22.462 --> 02:24:24.157
The committee was enchanted.

02:24:24.364 --> 02:24:27.527
- What did they say?
- I have never heard such enthusiasm.

02:24:27.801 --> 02:24:32.101
- Don't you think just this once...?
- Absolutely out of the question.

02:24:32.339 --> 02:24:36.469
- Georg, this is for Austria.
- For Austria?

02:24:36.843 --> 02:24:40.108
- There is no Austria!
- But the Anschluss was peaceful.

02:24:40.347 --> 02:24:43.805
- Let's at least be grateful for that.
- Grateful?

02:24:45.686 --> 02:24:47.347
You know, Max...

02:24:48.221 --> 02:24:51.486
...sometimes I don't believe
I know you.

02:24:54.161 --> 02:24:55.526
Father, I forgot.

02:24:56.363 --> 02:24:57.955
This is for you.

02:25:07.741 --> 02:25:11.734
Maria, he has got to at least pretend
to work with these people.

02:25:12.012 --> 02:25:13.536
You must convince him.

02:25:13.747 --> 02:25:16.511
Max, I can't ask him
to be less than he is.

02:25:16.750 --> 02:25:20.049
Then I'll talk to him.
If the children don't sing, well...

02:25:20.320 --> 02:25:22.550
...it will be a reflection
on Austria.

02:25:23.357 --> 02:25:26.724
Oh, I know.
It wouldn't do me any good either.

02:25:31.898 --> 02:25:34.560
Mother? That sounds so nice.

02:25:34.835 --> 02:25:37.565
- I like calling you "Mother."
- I like hearing it.

02:25:37.771 --> 02:25:41.502
You love Father very much.
I can tell you do.

02:25:41.708 --> 02:25:42.504
Very much.

02:25:42.776 --> 02:25:46.075
Mother, what do you do when you
think you love someone?

02:25:46.780 --> 02:25:52.082
I mean, when you stop loving someone
or he stops loving you?

02:25:54.688 --> 02:25:56.747
Well, you cry a little.

02:25:57.190 --> 02:25:59.283
Then you wait for the sun to come out.

02:25:59.593 --> 02:26:00.924
It always does.

02:26:01.194 --> 02:26:04.755
There are so many things I think
I should know but I don't.

02:26:04.965 --> 02:26:06.933
- I really don't.
- How can you?

02:26:07.200 --> 02:26:09.395
Sometimes I feel the world is ending.

02:26:09.636 --> 02:26:12.867
- Then you feel it's just beginning?
- Yes!

02:26:13.073 --> 02:26:17.305
It was that way with me. And for you
it will be just as wonderful.

02:26:17.978 --> 02:26:19.878
Do you really think so?

02:26:20.781 --> 02:26:24.717
<i>When you're 16 going on 17</i>

02:26:24.985 --> 02:26:28.580
<i>Waiting for life to start</i>

02:26:29.256 --> 02:26:33.090
<i>Somebody kind</i>
<i>Who touches your mind</i>

02:26:33.326 --> 02:26:37.626
<i>Will suddenly touch your heart</i>

02:26:38.065 --> 02:26:39.760
<i>When that happens</i>

02:26:40.233 --> 02:26:42.167
<i>After it happens</i>

02:26:42.402 --> 02:26:46.270
<i>Nothing is quite the same</i>

02:26:46.506 --> 02:26:48.064
<i>Somehow I know</i>

02:26:48.341 --> 02:26:50.468
<i>I'll jump up and go</i>

02:26:50.677 --> 02:26:54.977
<i>If ever he calls my name</i>

02:26:55.248 --> 02:26:59.150
<i>Gone are your old ideas of life</i>

02:26:59.419 --> 02:27:03.617
<i>The old ideas grow dim</i>

02:27:03.857 --> 02:27:08.260
<i>Lo and behold</i>
<i>You're someone's wife</i>

02:27:09.196 --> 02:27:15.192
<i>And you belong to him</i>

02:27:15.502 --> 02:27:19.802
<i>You may think this kind of adventure</i>

02:27:20.006 --> 02:27:23.874
<i>Never may come to you</i>

02:27:24.978 --> 02:27:30.348
<i>Darling, 16 going on 17</i>

02:27:31.184 --> 02:27:35.314
<i>Wait a year...</i>

02:27:36.123 --> 02:27:41.356
<i>- I'll wait a year</i>
<i>...or two</i>

02:27:41.795 --> 02:27:49.133
<i>Just wait a year...</i>

02:27:50.003 --> 02:27:58.638
<i>...or two</i>

02:28:01.047 --> 02:28:02.639
Liesl.

02:28:19.099 --> 02:28:20.430
What is it?

02:28:21.368 --> 02:28:22.733
Berlin.

02:28:23.203 --> 02:28:25.068
They've offered me a commission.

02:28:25.338 --> 02:28:27.863
I've been requested
to accept immediately...

02:28:28.108 --> 02:28:32.101
...and report to their naval base
at Bremerhaven tomorrow.

02:28:32.712 --> 02:28:36.705
I knew this would happen.
I didn't think it would be so soon.

02:28:36.950 --> 02:28:40.442
To refuse them would be fatal
for all of us.

02:28:41.688 --> 02:28:45.454
And joining them would be unthinkable.

02:28:51.631 --> 02:28:53.394
Get the children all together.

02:28:53.733 --> 02:28:56.930
Don't say anything to worry them.
Just get them ready.

02:28:57.904 --> 02:29:00.270
We've got to get out of Austria...

02:29:01.942 --> 02:29:03.603
...and this house...

02:29:05.946 --> 02:29:07.379
...tonight.

02:29:51.291 --> 02:29:53.691
This strains my back
and breaks my heart...

02:29:53.960 --> 02:29:56.793
...when I think of the children
missing the festival.

02:29:57.097 --> 02:29:59.759
By your announcement
we'll be over the border.

02:30:00.000 --> 02:30:02.434
Do you appreciate
the sacrifice I'm making?

02:30:02.636 --> 02:30:03.933
You have no choice.

02:30:04.170 --> 02:30:07.003
I know. That's why I'm making it.

02:30:07.707 --> 02:30:09.834
Why doesn't Father turn the motor on?

02:30:10.043 --> 02:30:13.479
Because he doesn't want anyone
to hear us.

02:30:17.117 --> 02:30:19.551
What will Frau Schmidt and Franz say?

02:30:19.819 --> 02:30:23.346
They'll be able to answer honestly
they didn't know anything.

02:30:23.556 --> 02:30:27.788
- Will we be coming back here?
- Someday, Liesl. I do hope someday.

02:30:28.028 --> 02:30:32.965
Are Father and Uncle Max going to push
the car all the way to Switzerland?

02:30:59.759 --> 02:31:02.159
Something wrong
with your car, captain?

02:31:02.495 --> 02:31:04.759
Yes, we couldn't get it started.

02:31:08.535 --> 02:31:09.763
Karl.

02:31:11.738 --> 02:31:15.230
Fix Captain von Trapp's car
so that it will start.

02:31:38.431 --> 02:31:40.228
Excellent, Karl.

02:31:43.603 --> 02:31:46.766
I've not asked you where you
and your family are going.

02:31:47.273 --> 02:31:49.400
Nor have you asked me why I'm here.

02:31:49.609 --> 02:31:53.375
Apparently we both suffer
from a deplorable lack of curiosity.

02:31:54.247 --> 02:31:56.715
You never answered the telegram...

02:31:56.950 --> 02:32:00.249
...from the Admiral of the Navy
of the Third Reich.

02:32:00.487 --> 02:32:02.955
I was under the impression,
Herr Zeller...

02:32:03.223 --> 02:32:06.715
...that the contents of telegrams
in Austria are private!

02:32:07.427 --> 02:32:10.954
At least, the Austria I know.

02:32:12.098 --> 02:32:13.725
I have my orders...

02:32:13.967 --> 02:32:16.128
...to take you
to Bremerhaven tonight...

02:32:16.403 --> 02:32:18.598
...where you will accept
your commission.

02:32:19.739 --> 02:32:25.177
I'm afraid that's going to be
quite impossible.

02:32:25.779 --> 02:32:27.508
You see, we...

02:32:28.081 --> 02:32:30.914
...all of us, the entire family,
will be...

02:32:31.985 --> 02:32:34.010
...singing in the festival tonight.

02:32:34.320 --> 02:32:36.788
As a matter of fact, we're going now.

02:32:37.424 --> 02:32:40.291
We couldn't possibly
let them down now.

02:32:40.493 --> 02:32:43.462
- I just hope we're not too late.
- Yes.

02:32:43.696 --> 02:32:46.597
You ask me to believe that you,
Captain von Trapp...

02:32:46.833 --> 02:32:48.300
...are singing in a concert?

02:32:48.701 --> 02:32:52.831
Believe me, it will be a performance
beyond anything even I've dreamt of.

02:32:53.206 --> 02:32:57.836
Like you, Herr Zeller,
I, too, am a man of hidden talents.

02:32:58.545 --> 02:32:59.876
Yes.

02:33:00.146 --> 02:33:02.637
Here, program.

02:33:07.654 --> 02:33:09.986
It says only the names
of the children.

02:33:10.223 --> 02:33:13.488
It says
the von Trapp Family Singers...

02:33:13.726 --> 02:33:16.786
...and I am the head of
the von Trapp family, am I not?

02:33:19.065 --> 02:33:22.865
And these travel clothes
that you're all wearing?

02:33:23.703 --> 02:33:25.227
Our costumes, naturally.

02:33:25.505 --> 02:33:28.906
This night air is not good
for the children's voices.

02:33:35.148 --> 02:33:38.675
Well, a slight delay in my orders
will not be serious.

02:33:39.886 --> 02:33:41.410
Therefore...

02:33:42.255 --> 02:33:43.882
...you will sing.

02:33:44.824 --> 02:33:46.815
You will all sing.

02:33:47.193 --> 02:33:49.718
But only because that's what I want.

02:33:50.663 --> 02:33:54.099
It will demonstrate that nothing
in Austria has changed.

02:33:54.834 --> 02:33:57.029
And when you have finished singing...

02:33:57.337 --> 02:34:00.500
...you, Captain von Trapp, will be
taken to Bremerhaven.

02:34:01.774 --> 02:34:04.504
Now, if you will all get
into your car...

02:34:04.744 --> 02:34:08.578
...we will escort the von Trapp Family
Singers to the festival.

02:34:09.449 --> 02:34:11.610
No escort will be necessary.

02:34:11.851 --> 02:34:14.342
Necessary? A pleasure, captain.

02:34:15.255 --> 02:34:19.123
After all, we would not want you
to get lost in the crowds.

02:34:20.360 --> 02:34:21.850
Would we?

02:34:22.529 --> 02:34:23.689
No.

02:34:39.913 --> 02:34:43.076
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

02:34:43.283 --> 02:34:46.480
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

02:34:46.753 --> 02:34:50.211
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

02:34:50.423 --> 02:34:54.223
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

02:35:03.803 --> 02:35:05.964
<i>Tea with jam</i>
<i>Jam and bread</i>

02:35:11.844 --> 02:35:15.177
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- A, B, C</i>

02:35:15.415 --> 02:35:18.646
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- Do-re-mi</i>

02:35:18.851 --> 02:35:22.446
<i>Tea with jam and bread</i>

02:35:22.689 --> 02:35:24.020
<i>With jam and bread</i>

02:35:24.290 --> 02:35:25.814
<i>With jam</i>
<i>With jam...</i>

02:35:26.025 --> 02:35:34.831
<i>...and bread</i>

02:35:56.823 --> 02:35:59.951
My fellow Austrians...

02:36:01.227 --> 02:36:05.789
...I shall not be seeing you again,
perhaps for a very long time.

02:36:07.200 --> 02:36:08.861
I would like to sing for you now...

02:36:10.470 --> 02:36:12.028
...a love song.

02:36:14.007 --> 02:36:16.202
I know you share this love.

02:36:17.510 --> 02:36:21.207
I pray that you will never let it die.

02:36:33.993 --> 02:36:37.520
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:37.730 --> 02:36:40.927
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:41.200 --> 02:36:46.934
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

02:36:47.340 --> 02:36:50.400
<i>Small and white</i>

02:36:50.677 --> 02:36:53.441
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:36:54.013 --> 02:36:59.110
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:36:59.886 --> 02:37:01.911
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:02.188 --> 02:37:05.783
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:06.025 --> 02:37:11.691
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:37:13.199 --> 02:37:15.690
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:15.935 --> 02:37:18.563
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:18.771 --> 02:37:24.767
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:37:29.282 --> 02:37:32.376
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:32.618 --> 02:37:33.949
<i>Edel...</i>

02:37:41.327 --> 02:37:44.421
<i>Small and white</i>

02:37:44.630 --> 02:37:47.497
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:37:47.734 --> 02:37:53.070
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:53.906 --> 02:37:55.874
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:56.075 --> 02:37:59.476
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:38:00.146 --> 02:38:06.142
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:38:06.619 --> 02:38:09.520
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:09.822 --> 02:38:12.586
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:13.192 --> 02:38:21.429
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:38:39.152 --> 02:38:40.710
I think it'll work.

02:38:41.454 --> 02:38:43.217
I shall miss all of you.

02:38:43.723 --> 02:38:46.157
I shall miss the money
I could have made with you.

02:38:49.562 --> 02:38:51.120
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

02:38:51.864 --> 02:38:54.526
The competition has come
to its conclusion...

02:38:54.801 --> 02:38:57.895
...except, we don't know
yet what that conclusion will be.

02:38:58.871 --> 02:39:01.396
And while the judges
arrive at their decision...

02:39:01.674 --> 02:39:04.700
...I have been given permission
to offer you an encore.

02:39:04.977 --> 02:39:08.174
This will be the last opportunity
the von Trapps will have...

02:39:08.414 --> 02:39:10.814
...of singing together
for a long, long time.

02:39:11.884 --> 02:39:15.877
Even now, officials are waiting
in this auditorium...

02:39:16.155 --> 02:39:18.885
...to escort Captain von Trapp
to his new command...

02:39:19.091 --> 02:39:22.652
...in the naval forces
of the Third Reich.

02:39:27.333 --> 02:39:31.861
And so, ladies and gentlemen,
the family von Trapp again...

02:39:32.505 --> 02:39:34.769
...to bid you farewell.

02:39:42.014 --> 02:39:45.609
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

02:39:45.885 --> 02:39:49.218
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

02:39:49.722 --> 02:39:53.590
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

02:39:53.793 --> 02:39:56.227
<i>Is popping out to say "coo-coo"</i>

02:39:56.429 --> 02:39:58.090
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:58.364 --> 02:39:59.353
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:59.632 --> 02:40:01.224
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

02:40:01.434 --> 02:40:03.231
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

02:40:03.469 --> 02:40:06.233
<i>To say goodbye</i>

02:40:06.439 --> 02:40:11.604
<i>To you</i>

02:40:14.580 --> 02:40:18.107
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

02:40:18.384 --> 02:40:22.115
<i>We hate to go</i>
<i>And miss this pretty sight</i>

02:40:28.294 --> 02:40:31.889
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

02:40:32.098 --> 02:40:35.761
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

02:40:42.074 --> 02:40:45.669
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:45.912 --> 02:40:47.504
<i>We flit, we float</i>

02:40:47.780 --> 02:40:49.441
<i>We fleetly flee, we fly</i>

02:40:55.821 --> 02:40:59.621
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:59.825 --> 02:41:03.192
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>
<i>And so must I</i>

02:41:03.462 --> 02:41:07.262
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:07.500 --> 02:41:13.200
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:13.439 --> 02:41:18.638
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:18.878 --> 02:41:26.046
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:57.850 --> 02:42:01.980
Ladies and gentlemen, I have here the
decision of our distinguished judges.

02:42:02.188 --> 02:42:04.748
We will start with the award
for third prize.

02:42:05.391 --> 02:42:07.723
For this honor,
the judges have named...

02:42:07.994 --> 02:42:12.590
...the first soloist of the choir
of St. Agatha's Church in Murback.

02:42:12.865 --> 02:42:15.095
Fräulein Schweiger.

02:42:52.038 --> 02:42:55.974
Second prize
to The Toby Reiser Quintet.

02:43:23.936 --> 02:43:28.100
And the first prize,
the highest honor in all Austria...

02:43:28.340 --> 02:43:31.434
...the von Trapp Family Singers.

02:43:43.823 --> 02:43:45.484
The family von Trapp.

02:44:00.106 --> 02:44:01.164
They're gone!

02:44:19.859 --> 02:44:21.292
Come with me.

02:44:25.131 --> 02:44:27.122
Quickly, quickly.

02:44:28.033 --> 02:44:30.228
I have a place you can hide.

02:44:30.970 --> 02:44:34.235
Slowly, slowly.

02:44:45.217 --> 02:44:46.912
Open this gate.

02:44:48.053 --> 02:44:49.645
Good evening.

02:44:52.158 --> 02:44:53.591
Hurry up, woman.

02:45:13.445 --> 02:45:14.707
Two men in there.

02:45:14.914 --> 02:45:16.779
Six of you cover the yard.

02:45:17.016 --> 02:45:19.246
You two, cover the corridor.

02:45:33.732 --> 02:45:37.293
Reverend Mother, we didn't realize
we put the abbey in this danger.

02:45:37.570 --> 02:45:40.095
No, Maria, it was right for you
to come here.

02:45:40.306 --> 02:45:42.206
We thought we might borrow
your car.

02:45:42.408 --> 02:45:44.308
I'm afraid our car will do you
no good now.

02:45:44.910 --> 02:45:46.571
I've been listening to the wires.

02:45:46.779 --> 02:45:49.304
The borders have just been closed.

02:45:55.154 --> 02:45:57.452
All right,
if the borders are closed...

02:45:58.757 --> 02:46:02.056
...then we'll drive up into the hills
and go over the mountains on foot.

02:46:02.661 --> 02:46:04.652
- The children...
- We'll help them.

02:46:04.930 --> 02:46:07.091
We can do it without help, Father.

02:46:08.133 --> 02:46:09.498
Maria.

02:46:10.236 --> 02:46:12.830
You will not be alone.
Remember:

02:46:13.072 --> 02:46:16.166
"I will lift up mine eyes unto
the hills from whence cometh my help."

02:46:17.142 --> 02:46:18.234
Yes, Mother.

02:46:19.612 --> 02:46:21.773
- I'm scared.
- Me too.

02:46:33.859 --> 02:46:35.019
God be with you.

02:46:41.967 --> 02:46:43.525
- Mother.
- Yes?

02:46:43.769 --> 02:46:46.966
Would it help if we sang
about our favorite things?

02:46:47.206 --> 02:46:50.198
No, darling.
This is one time it would not help.

02:46:50.476 --> 02:46:53.673
You must be very quiet.
Hold tight to me.

02:49:08.347 --> 02:49:09.575
Let's try the roof.

02:50:05.838 --> 02:50:08.068
Rolfe, please.

02:50:13.178 --> 02:50:14.668
No, wait.

02:50:24.490 --> 02:50:25.821
Maria.

02:50:26.892 --> 02:50:28.325
Children.

02:50:32.364 --> 02:50:35.390
It's you we want, not them.

02:50:35.767 --> 02:50:37.496
Put that down.

02:50:38.570 --> 02:50:41.869
Not another move,
or I'll shoot.

02:50:43.575 --> 02:50:45.600
You're only a boy.

02:50:48.614 --> 02:50:52.277
- You don't really belong to them.
- Stay where you are.

02:50:54.052 --> 02:50:56.043
Come away with us.

02:50:57.289 --> 02:50:58.449
Before it's too late.

02:50:59.057 --> 02:51:01.389
Not another step.
I'll kill you.

02:51:03.695 --> 02:51:07.028
- You give that to me, Rolfe.
- Did you hear me?

02:51:08.033 --> 02:51:09.591
I'll kill you.

02:51:11.470 --> 02:51:12.937
Rolfe.

02:51:31.323 --> 02:51:32.654
You'll never be one of them.

02:51:35.427 --> 02:51:37.122
Lieutenant!

02:51:37.396 --> 02:51:38.522
They're here!

02:51:38.730 --> 02:51:40.288
They're here, lieutenant!

02:52:21.607 --> 02:52:23.268
Reverend Mother.

02:52:24.543 --> 02:52:26.374
I have sinned.

02:52:27.546 --> 02:52:29.707
I too, Reverend Mother.

02:52:31.350 --> 02:52:33.682
What is this sin, my children?

